    "description": "The Prague Zoo is located in the beautiful rugged terrain of The Troja basin.\r\n\r\nThe history of Prague Zoo goes all the way back to the year 1881, when, on the occasion of the wedding of Crown Prince Rudolf and Princess Stephanie of Belgium, Count Sweerts-Sporck published an open letter in the newspapers calling for the establishment of a zoological garden in Prague.\r\n\r\nIn 1931 the ZOO opened its door to the public counting 200 animals. Nowadays it boasts 670 species and over 5000 living specimens. The area of ZOO is 58 ha, with total exhibit area 50 ha. In 2007 Prague ZOO was listed among 8 best zoological gardens in the world, in 2015 according to Trip Advisor users, it ranked 4th among world´s ZOOs.",
