    "description": "Karlovy Vary was founded in the 14th century. Legend said that the Czech King and Emperor Charles IV. had discovered a hot spring during hunting. After finding out that this hot spring is healing, he had a city built. About 300 years later, Karlovy Vary was already world-famous spa town, where the nobility and the rich European cultural elite came to heal and relax there. Karlovy Vary was visited by many famous personalities such as Tsar Peter the Great, Emperor Franz Joseph I, the poet J.W. Goethe, the composer W.A. Mozart and many more. Nowadays Karlovy Vary is still the most popular Czech spa town. You should not miss Jan Becher Museum, the Moser glass factory or The International Film Festival. Do not forget to taste the famous Karlovy Vary wafers.\r\n\r\nJan Becher Museum: \r\nOne of the most famous products of Karlovy Vary is the herbal liqueur Becherovka, which is also referred as the 13th healing spring. Jan Becher had the factory, now connected with the museum built in 1867. Do you know exactly how many herbs contain this unique drink? Come smell the ingredients and uncover a secret of production of this delicious liqueur!  During the guided route you will see the historical exhibits, historical cellars and in the museum bar you will see the film about history and present production and what else you have a great opportunity to taste Becherovka liqueur.​\r\nwww.becherovka.cz",
    "tourProgramExample": "Tours for the Jan Becher museum are available in German, Czech and English.",
    "officialWebsite": "https://www.karlovyvary.cz/en",
    "capacityMin": 1,
    "capacityMax": 40,
    "capacityDetails": "Capacity is based on maximum pax for the visit of Becherovka museum, bigger groups can be organized and split into smaller ones for this visit.",
