    "description": "Karlovy Vary was founded in the 14th century. Legend said that the Czech King and Emperor Charles IV. had discovered a hot spring during hunting. After finding out that this hot spring is healing, he had a city built. About 300 years later, Karlovy Vary was already world-famous spa town, where the nobility and the rich European cultural elite came to heal and relax there. \r\n\r\nKarlovy Vary was visited by many famous personalities such as Tsar Peter the Great, Emperor Franz Joseph I, the poet J.W. Goethe, the composer W.A. Mozart and many more. Nowadays Karlovy Vary is still the most popular Czech spa town. You should not miss Jan Becher Museum, the Moser glass factory or The International Film Festival. Do not forget to taste the famous Karlovy Vary wafers.\r\n\r\nMoser Glass Factory and Museum: In the place where Moser crystal is born, you will experience the true atmosphere of handmade glassmaking, smell the baked wooden forms and breathe more than 160 years of history. You can visit the glassworks, sales gallery or museum, where we present the story of the glassworks from the oldest works to current collections.",
    "tourProgramExample": "TOUR OF THE GLASSWORKS\r\nYou will get acquainted with the creative manual work of glass masters. You will see how they transform a hot mass of glass pulled from a hot furnace into a work of art, how they blow and shape glass in wooden forms. The tour also includes a visit to the Moser Museum. Language: Czech, English, after telephone agreement also German, Ukrainian, Russian\r\n\r\nVIP TOUR OF MOSER GLASSWORKS\r\nYou will take a look behind the scenes of the glassworks and the secrets of crystal glass creation. You will get to know the glassworks, which is the heart of every glassworks, you will visit the cutting, moulding and engraving workshop. Seeing the entire process of glass creation up close is an unrepeatable experience that a regular tour does not offer. Language: Czech, English, after telephone agreement also German, Ukrainian, Russian\r\n\r\nCREATIVE TOUR\r\nYou will take a look behind the scenes of the glassworks and the secrets of crystal glass creation. You will get to know the glassworks, which is the heart of every glassworks, you will visit the cutting, moulding and engraving workshop. Seeing the entire process of glass creation up close is an unrepeatable experience that a regular tour does not offer. In addition, under the supervision of a master engraver, you will try the engraving craft. We will dedicate the original motif engraved by your hand on Moser crystal as a memento of your visit. Language: Czech, English, after telephone agreement also German, Ukrainian, Russian\r\n\r\nGOLDEN TOUR\r\nYou will take a look behind the scenes of the glassworks and the secrets of crystal glass creation. You will get to know the glassworks, which is the heart of every glassworks, and visit the cutting and moulding workshop. In addition, you will try 2 decorating techniques yourself – first you sand the selected motif on a glass and then decorate the contours yourself with 24 carat gold. The glass will then go through firing and we will deliver it to your home within 3 working days. In addition to memories, you will be left with an original self-decorated glass. Commentary language: Czech, English",
    "officialWebsite": "https://www.moser.com/cs/o-moseru/prohlidka-sklarny",
    "capacityMin": 0,
    "capacityMax": 0,
    "capacityDetails": "Capacity depends on which tour:\r\nTour of Glassworks: Tour group: maximum 2023 people\r\nVIP Tour of Moser Glassworks: Tour group: maximum 5 people\r\nCreative Tour: Tour group: maximum 5 people\r\nGolden Tour: Tour group: maximum 5 persons",
