    "description": "You surely must have heard about Pilsner Urquell – known as one of the best beers in the world. Would you like to see and learn how beer is brewed? We invite you to visit the largest brewery in the Czech Republic.\r\n\r\nDuring the guided tour you will learn about the history and secret of production of the legendary Pilsner Urquell. You will visit the authentic places where beer has been brewed since 1842 and also the modern bottling plant and brew house. \r\n\r\nFinally the beer tasting is waiting for you in the historical cellars, where you can taste the unfiltered and unpasteurised Pilsner Urquell tapped directly from the oak barrels.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Beer lovers will surely be captivated by the historic cellars, where Pilsner Urquell beer is still produced using the traditional method of the first brewer. We will explain to you the unique brewing process of Pilsner Urquell beer, which is identical to the one introduced by Josef Groll in 1842. The highlight of the tour is the tasting of unfiltered and unpasteurized Pilsner Urquell beer drawn directly from oak lager barrels in historical cellars.\r\n\r\nFrom the courtyard of the brewery we will also take you by brewery bus to a tour of the bottling room, which is one of the most modern in Europe and its capacity is an impressive 120,000 bottles per hour.\r\n\r\nBrewery tour:\r\nVisitor Centre\r\nBottling plant\r\nExposure of raw materials\r\nVarna\r\nPeople from Pilsner Urquell\r\nBrewery cellars\r\nTasting of unfiltered beer from oak lager barrels",
