    "description": "Sold in 30 countries around the world to-date, Velkopopovicky Kozel is a Czech lager produced since 1874.\r\n\r\nFounded South-East of Prague, the brewery has taken its trademark in a symbol of a male goat (hence the name \"Kozel\", which stands for this animal). \r\n\r\nThe brewery was finally sold to Asahi Breweries in 2016, yet keeping the local flavor and quality, You can safely enjoy the tour of the brewery along with beer tasting and some queries perhaps about how to become a good bar and beer tender? Who can tell?",
