    "description": "The beginning of Loreto Church dates back to 1626. It was enlarged throughout the 17th and 18th centuries to create a complex of buildings surrounding the central Santa Casa (Holy House), i.e. the house that witnessed the moment of Incarnation of Jesus.\r\n\r\nThe concept of Loreto in Prague is actually a reflection of the original pattern of the Italian Loreto destroyed by fire in 1921. \r\n\r\nBesides the Santa Casa, the complex includes The Church of the Nativity of Our Lord, the arcade courtyard with several chapels and the treasury with religious relics. Visitors passing by Loreto may also hear its wonderful carillon placed here at the end of the 17th century, playing on the hour to encourage the pilgrims for prayers.  ​",
