    "description": "Lesser Town is one of the most wonderful and oldest parts of Prague. This place stretched on the slops below Prague Castle, was settled in 10th century. \r\n​\r\nThe town itself was founded in 1257. In the Renaissance and Baroque period the nobles ordered to build their palaces here. The baroque church of St. Nicolas became a landmark of this location.\r\n\r\nYou also will visit the most popular pilgrimage place in Prague – The Church of Our Lady Victorious that is also located at Lesser Town. Inside the Church the famous Infant Jesus is located, the 16th century wax-coated wooden statue of the Child Jesus holding a globus cruciger of Spanish Origin.",
