    "description": "No history of Denmark is complete without the Vikings - the fierce warriors whose bloody adventures influenced all of Europe over a 1000 years ago.​\r\n​\r\nRoskilde dates back to the Viking era and is famous for its Viking Ship Museum, which hold the remains of 5 well-preserved Viking ships.​\r\n\r\nThe museum tells the story of how the Vikings changed the World with their ships.​\r\n\r\nAt Roskilde Viking Ship Museum, the group will enjoy an inside guided visit hearing all the exciting stories about the famous Viking ships, which stand beautifully – but silently – on display, keeping their secrets about a distant past with terrifying Viking raids and trading voyages to far-away shores, about the seafarers on board and their life by the sea almost 1,000 years ago.​\r\n\r\nThe visit can be combined with workshops or sailing on the Roskilde fjord.",
