    "description": "Visit the place that is Karen Blixen's childhood home, and experience the atmosphere in the living rooms where well-known and beloved stories came to be.\r\n\r\nA writer's childhood home\r\n\"Babette's Guest\", \"The African Farm\", \"Seven Fantastic Tales\". Pearls in Danish literature and all written and recorded in the house Rungstedlund by Rungsted Strand. With the home where she lived and wrote, and the exhibitions of books, letters and art, the Karen Blixen Museum provides the story of one of Denmark's greatest and most famous authors.\r\n\r\nThe museum inspires and has been featured in magazines such as Vogue.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.voguescandinavia.com/articles/connie-nielsen-talks-playing-karen-blixen\r\n\r\nAnd of course the famous movie: \"Out of Africa\"\r\n\r\nhttps://www.vogue.fr/fashion-culture/article/out-of-africa-anecdotes-fun-facts-to-know-movie",
