    "description": "Stevns Klint is a white chalk cliff located on the southern end of the island of Zealand. It was named a UNESCO world heritage site in 2014.\r\n\r\nIt is known as one of the best exposed Cretaceous - Terriary boundaries in the world. Stevns Klint is the only place on earth to find traces of a global environmental disaster that happened about 65 million years ago. The climate changed drastically and almost 75% of all animal species and 60% of all plants became extinct.\r\n\r\nStevn Klint is good place for a little walk and visit to local museum Cold War museum with its WWII dungeons.",
