    "description": "Carlsberg has everything a good story is made of. A dramatic family saga, entrepreneurship, large capital, and an irrepressible faith in the future. Combined with a sense of quality, art and architecture, the brewing family Jacobsen has left a big mark on all of Copenhagen. It was on Valby Bakke that it all began more than 150 years ago.\r\n\r\nToday, Carlsberg is no longer an industrial district, but an urban district. Much has been demolished, some is preserved and remained, and others are transformed and reused.\r\n\r\nWe take the tour around Carlsberg Byen, and talk about the area’s historical weight, about the comprehensive plan that is the basis for the entire new development, and we will look at how sustainability and climate protection are planned.\r\n\r\nCome with us and get an insight into the homes, hotels, institutions, squares and roads that shape the new Carlsberg Byen.",
