    "description": "Sonderborg Castle was constructed as a fortefied tower by Valdemar the Great in 1158. It played a large role in the struggle between the King of Denmark and the Duke of Schloneswig over the ownership of the area.\r\n\r\nThe Castle now houses a museum cronicling the history of the south Jutland region from the middle ages through present day, with special focus on  the Schleswig wars of 1848-1850 and 1864, World War II and the Reunification of 1920.",
