    "description": "The Raeapteek (Town Hall Pharmacy) is the oldest pharmacy in Europe that has continuously been in business in the same building. The exact opening date is not known, but in 1422 the pharmacy already had its third owner. In 2022, 600 years passed since the first written mentioning in the town council book. \r\n\r\nThis pharmacy is one of the most popular sightseeing spots in Tallinn Old Town.\r\n\r\nThe workshop starts with the tour in the Raeapteek museum introducing the history of the pharmacy and Medieval treating methods.\r\n\r\nMarzipan workshop involves mixing together the primary ingredients and decorating the readymade product. Everyone is welcome to take their marzipan home.\r\n\r\nThe group for this workshop can not be bigger than 10 people. Claret degustation available, price added to the workshop.",
