    "description": "Spend time exploring some of Helsinki’s most impressive landmarks in a company of a local guide that will host you during this tour. \r\n\r\nDuring your walking tour you will pass by the charming Katajanokka district well know by its Art Nouveau architectural buildings, Here you will view the green-and-gold-domed Russian Orthodox Uspenski Cathedral, walk through the famous open air market square and stop to admire the historical Senate Square with its Neo-Classical atmosphere and surrounded by Helsinki’s monumental  main Lutheran Cathedral, the Senate building and the University of Helsinki. \r\n\r\nTour continues towards the Railway Station, another symbol of the Finnish National Romantic architecture. From the Station’s perimeter you will have a good view from Helsinki’s National Theater and National Gallery.   From there a short walk to view architectural gems like the Oodi library, Music centre and Parliament buildings.\r\n\r\nTour ends in city centre or back at your hotel.",
