    "description": "A visit to Finland is only completed if one enjoys the most recommended “Do like the locals” experience – enjoying a Sauna!\r\n\r\nLöyly, the most famous public sauna in Helsinki is the spot to be if one wishes to go for a sauna while enjoying the stunning views of the Finnish capital archipelago.  This modern seaside sauna with a stylish, glass-walled restaurant & large deck for sweeping views standing by the Baltic Sea has featured in Time Magazine´s “World 100 Greatest Places”.    \r\n\r\nThe venue has 2 saunas: traditional smoke sauna and wood-burning sauna  (for appr. 20 pax/sauna), swimming possibility for those that ”dare” to for a swim in the Baltic sea. In winter time, it is even more thrilling when the sea is ”frozen” and water temperature close ranging negative temperature.\r\n\r\nTogether with the public sauna, groups can also privatize own sauna. The private sauna is best for a maximum group of 10 persons at a time. Bigger group needs to revise. Private sauna also allows use of the public saunas.",
