    "description": "Embracing the stamp of sustainability, Lonna has the  Good Travel Seal certificate and based on that they have been assigned Sustainable Travel Finland label, starting February 2023.\r\n\r\nLonna’s restaurant is open during the summer, serving our island guests from May until the end of September. The restaurant serves high-quality seasonal dishes with a modern take on traditional island cuisine. They strive to use mostly Finnish ingredients, favoring organic and locally grown produce, always knowing the origin. \r\n\r\nIt is also possible to organize inspiring meetings on the island of Lonna. Within a 10 min. ferry ride away from the city center you could be unleashing your creativity in a fantastic marine environment. There are facilities on the island for smaller team meetings and for the larger seminars too.\r\n\r\nThis visit can be combined with own privatized cruise around the archipelago or island hoping for a guided tour to the UNESCO Heritage site – the Fortress Island of Suomenlinna.",
