    "description": "At the Nuuksio National Park visitors can enjoy autumn in local “Finnish” way. The trees in the forest would be coloured up with beautiful autumn leaves - which is called “Ruska” in Finnish.\r\n\r\nEveryman's Right in Finland gives all people whether residing in Finland or just visiting the right to enjoy nature anywhere in the Finnish countryside regardless of land ownership. Therefore, this Everyman's Right allows all visitors to pick berries and mushrooms almost everywhere without any charge!\r\n\r\nThe best way to enjoy picking up berries and mushrooms in the forest would be definitely a joining a berry/mushroom picking tour into the forest with nature guide - so that professional nature guide will teach you about the berries/mushrooms that we can collect and taste on the day.",
