    "description": "3 GOOD REASONS TO VISIT !\r\n• A site with an impressive history \r\nand spectacular architecture.\r\n• The motherhouse of almost 1,500 Cluniac sites \r\nacross Europe.\r\n• The restored chapel of Jean de Bourbon\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Benedictine abbey of Cluny was founded in 910 and extended its influence over the centuries throughout Europe \r\nthanks to the extraordinary scale of its church. \r\n\r\nExplore the remains of the great 11th-century church, \r\nwhich was partly destroyed after the French Revolution, \r\nalong with the many monastic buildings at the site, \r\nincluding the Galileo passage with its reliquaries and coin \r\ntreasures, the 18th-century cloister, the chapterhouse, the \r\n13th-century granary, the framework of which houses the \r\ncapitals of the great church, the cellar, the Palais Jean de \r\nBourbon and the museum of art and archaeology.",
    "tourProgramExample": "- SELF-GUIDED TOUR: \r\nWith guide booklet. \r\nReservation required. Duration: 1hr30.\r\nMaximum group size: 40 people\r\n\r\n- AUDIO-GUIDE TOUR: \r\nReservation required. Duration: 1hr30. \r\n\r\n- LECTURE TOUR OF THE ABBEY AND/OR MUSEUM\r\nChoice of themes\r\nReservation required. Duration: from 1hr30 to 2hrs30\r\n\r\n- PRIVATE TOUR: \r\nExplore the abbey outside of opening hours, with or without catering. \r\nReservation required. Duration: 2hrs.",
    "officialWebsite": "https://www.cluny-abbaye.fr/en",
