    "description": "In collaboration with the Wine House at Chambord, participants are introduced to the diversity of the vineyard and the richness of the terroir through the \r\ndiscovery of 3 wines from the AOC of Cheverny and Cour-Cheverny.\r\n\r\nThe AOC Cour-Cheverny is produced from a single variety the \"Romorantin\", introduced in the Loire Valley by François I and planted about thirty kilometers \r\nfrom Chambord, near the chateau of Romorantin.\r\n\r\nThese wines will no longer have secrets for the group. \r\nThe Loire Valley is the 3rd largest appellation region in France, with a total of 85 appellations and denominations. The area has been awarded UNESCO World Heritage status – one of only ten European winegrowing regions distinguished in this way.",
