    "description": "Located in the south of Burgundy, the Cave de Chaintré is one of the oldest cooperative wineries in France. Established in 1928 on the site of an ancient Gallo-Roman villa, it brings together a group of winegrowers who passionately cultivate Chardonnay, the region's emblematic grape variety. \r\n\r\nThe Chaintré winery has undergone several stages of investment, enabling the acquisition of appropriate technical equipment to ensure, in particular, the temperature control essential to the production of white wines.\r\n\r\nThe Chaintré winery is evolving and innovating with a new tasting and sales area at its production site. Visitors will be able to discover all the wines produced by the winery, as well as regional products, in a warm, modern setting.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Package “Découverte” - 1h30 / 2h\r\n- Group Reception\r\n- Cellar Tour (Presentation of the history, the vineyard and the\r\ncellar)\r\n- Video projection of a 15 minutes film about the cellar\r\n- Commented tasting of 4/5 wines\r\n\r\nPackage “Gourmand” - 1h30 / 2h\r\n- Group Reception\r\n- Cellar Tour (Presentation of the history, the vineyard and the cellar)\r\n- Video projection of a 15 minutes film about the cellar\r\n- Commented tasting of 4/5 wines\r\n- “Mâchon Beaujolais” : Local cheeses and charcuterie to accompany the tasting\r\n\r\nPackage “Prestige” - 1h30 / 2h\r\n- Group Reception\r\n- Cellar Tour (Presentation of the history, the vineyard and the cellar)\r\n- Video projection of a 15 minutes film about the cellar\r\n- Commented tasting of 4/5 wines\r\n- “Mâchon Beaujolais” : Local cheeses and charcuterie to accompany the tasting\r\n- Goodies Juliénas Chaintré Vignerons Associés (3€) or a bottle of wine as a gift\r\n(10€).",
