    "description": "With an exceptional geographical location, unfolding onto the English Channel and at the gateway to the European cities of Paris and London, with 600 kilometres of coastline, fabulous countryside and several UNESCO world heritage listed sites including Mont-Saint-Michel, Normandy welcomes you year round with open arms!\r\n\r\nAdmire Mont Saint-Michel bay, contemplate the water lilies in Monet’s gardens at Giverny, climb the Etretat cliffs, stroll along the beautiful pedestrian streets in the centre of Rouen, discover Auguste Perret’s modern urbanism in Le Havre, go to the market at Honfleur, attend the Deauville American Film Festival, etc. There is so much to see and do in Normandy!",
