    "description": "The Chamonix-Mont-Blanc golf club is an 18-hole golf course at 1000 meters above sea level opened in 1934 in Les Praz de Chamonix. Its course, Chamonix is a par 72 of 5718 meters.\r\n\r\nLocated between the Mont Blanc Massif and the Aiguilles Rouges at the foot of the famous Drus, Chamonix Golf Club bears the prestigious signature of Robert Trent Jones Senior.\r\n\r\nYear of Establishment: The Chamonix Golf Course was created in 1934 with a 9-hole course and expanded to an 18-hole course in 1982 by architect Trent Jones Senior, under the initiative of Maurice Herzog. \r\n\r\nType of Course: A technically challenging yet stunningly beautiful course, recognized as one of the flattest mountain golf courses in the Alps. \r\n\r\nFacilities \r\n- Clubhouse: The ProShop is centrally located, dividing the course into two distinct parts with no long transfers required. \r\n- Practice Areas: Includes a driving range a few hundred meters from the reception area and several putting green training zones. \r\n- Parking: Public parking is available around the course. \r\n- Restaurant: \r\n- Bar-Restaurant: The Clubhouse “Le Chalet” is located in front of the 18th green. \r\n- Features: A sunny terrace with Mont Blanc views and a covered terrace. \r\n\r\nReservations: Managed by a separate company. Bookings can be made directly online for individuals.",
    "tourProgramExample": "",
    "officialWebsite": "https://www.maisondesdrus.com/en/",
    "capacityMin": 0,
