    "description": "Today the Château’s vineyards include seven rare Premier Cru blocks located entirely along the renowned Côte d’Or escarpment, home to some of the world’s most storied Pinot Noir and Chardonnay wines.\r\n\r\nComprising 25 acres of prime vineyard blocks in Pommard, Volnay, Meursault, Puligny-Montrachet, Chassagne-Montrachet, Santenay and Maranges, the Château de la Crée estate features a two-to-one varietal ratio of Pinot Noir to Chardonnay, with 40% of all plantings in Premier Cru sites. In conversion into an organic farming, the practices are employed in all our vineyards to drive optimal terroir expression, and ensure soil and plant health.\r\n\r\nMake the most of a stopover in Santenay to discover our wines and the exceptional terroirs of our appellation by tasting a selection of 5 of our wines in our 15th century cellars or on the terrace of the Château de la Crée, weather permitting.",
