    "description": "Located in a green enclosure a few steps from the centre of Reims, the Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix chapel appears to be a modest building, measuring seven by sixteen metres, in the tradition of country churches.\r\n\r\nThe artistic testament of the Franco-Japanese Léonard Foujita, the Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix chapel was designed and entirely decorated by the painter between 1965 and 1966.\r\n\r\nConverted to Christianity in Reims in 1959, he deployed his universe mixing his Japanese culture with references to the Italian Renaissance. Foujita and his wife Kimiyo are buried there.",
