    "description": "About Discover the Hôtel-Dieu des Hospices Civils de Beaune, a hospital founded in 1443 by Nicolas Rolin, Chancellor of the Dukes of Burgundy, and his wife Guigone de Salins.\r\n\r\nA charitable institution entrusted to the care of the hospital sisters, this \"palace for the poor\" dedicated to the homeless and the sick without resources remained in operation until 1971.\r\n\r\nKnown for its polychrome glazed terracotta roofs, the Hôtel-Dieu is also a major memorial to hospital history with its polyptych of the Last Judgment by Rogier van der Weyden, its treatment rooms, its kitchen, its apothecary, and its collections of furniture and art objects.",
