    "description": "The Mercedes-Benz Museum celebrates the automobile invented by Carl Benz in 1886: it relates its history and tells its stories, bringing both alive by placing them in the context of technology, day-to-day life, social history and popular culture.\r\n\r\nTogether with other exhibits, 160 vehicles of all types form the centrepiece of the permanent exhibition covering a total of 16,500 square metres.\r\n\r\nThis unparalleled world can be discovered on two tours that follow a \"Legend\" and \"Collection\" narrative.\r\n\r\nIt is not only the content of the Mercedes-Benz Museum that visitors find fascinating - but also the building that houses this history of innovation. Its unique design comes from the Dutch architect Ben van Berkel of UN Studio. He created a visionary building with walls and ceilings consisting of a double helix of highly individual components.",
