    "description": "Among Berlin's residential areas, one still stands out today: the Grunewald, conveniently located between City West and Berlin's most famous forest. Patronized by Chancellor Bismarck, wealthy Berliners settled here from 1889 onwards, enjoying the tranquility of their vast estates while also taking advantage of the proximity to Kurfürstendamm. Among the most famous residents were the industrialist and Foreign Minister Walther Rathenau, the publisher Samuel Fischer, the Mendelssohn banking family, as well as the dancer Isadora Duncan, the film director Friedrich Wilhelm Murnau, and the writers Vicki Baum and Hermann Sudermann.\r\n\r\nThe tour leads to the idyllic corners of the villa suburb, to preserved magnificent villas, picturesque lakes and places of small stories and great history.",
