    "description": "Visit the bohemian scene of the \"Golden 20s\" in the so-called \"New West\". Come with us to original locations, legendary literary meeting places, places where authors lived and worked.\r\n\r\nFrom Winterfeldtplatz to Nollendorfplatz, actor Eckehard Hoffmann takes us to 18 historic locations. You will visit the former Piscator Stage, the Nollendorf Casino and the \"Beautiful Unknown from Nollendorfplatz\". On site, Hoffmann recites prose, poetry and essays by Alfred Kerr, Ernst Weiß, Hans Fallada, Paul Scheerbart, Ernst Toller, among others. \"Lemke's Blessed Widow\" by Erdmann Gräser transports us to the old Berlin of the 19th century. \r\n\r\nExcerpts from the Göbbels speech in the former sports palace remind us of the Nazi regime's raw claim to power. And \"Woman and Socialism\" by August Bebel will surprise you in its topicality.",
