    "description": "Romantically located on the Havel River, Glienicke Villa appears like an Italian country villa. Designed by Karl Friedrich Schinkel for Prince Carl, Glienicke lets the visitor experience the beauty of Neoclassical architecture set in an exceptional park landscape that was created by Peter Joseph Lenné.\r\n\r\nThe preserved villa interiors are fascinating, often decorated in strong colors, such as the Red Hall and the library in deep blue. Although they are located on the Berlin side of the Havel, Glienicke Villa and Park are part of the Potsdam ensemble of palaces and gardens that belong to the UNESCO World Heritage.\r\n\r\nThe park offers the visitor numerous viewing axes, for instance to the Church of the Savior in Sacrow and to Peacock Island.",
