    "description": "Learn how to make the authentic roman-style pasta, fried seasonal specialties of the local tradition in a cozy restaurant in the Jewish area in Rome city Centre.\r\n\r\nA cooking class is a must-do when in Rome!\r\nTake a break from visiting the City meeting local people, learning how to make a typical Roman dinner menu from scratch.\r\n\r\nNo worries about the name “Ghetto”, this is one of the safest and charming area of Rome, beloved by locals and full of history.\r\nThough Rome’s Jewish Ghetto no longer officially exists, the neighborhood is still bearing the old name, and is the hearth of Rome’s Jewish community, the oldest in Italy.\r\n\r\nToday, despite its unhappy history, the Jewish Ghetto is now one of Rome’s most beautiful neighborhoods that worth to be visited in the easy-going happy lifestyle, which is famous for.\r\n\r\nThis is a hands-on class, but if you’d just like to be a spectator you can relax, watching her working, with a glass of wine.\r\nLearning history and legend around the Jewish quarter and its unique food style and lots of chatting.\r\n\r\nThe experience is suitable to everyone, not suitable for celiac. Can be alcohol free if requested. Kids are welcome",
    "tourProgramExample": "Meet your host in the amazing Piazza Mattei, in the hearth of the Jewish Ghetto of Rome.\r\nHead to the restaurant where the chef waits for you to reveal secrets and recipes.\r\nThis is a hands-on class, but if you’d just like to be a spectator you can relax, watching her working, with a glass of wine.\r\nLearning history and legend around the Jewish quarter and its unique food style and lots of chatting.",
