    "description": "The Mamertine Prison, or Carcer Tullianum, is the oldest prison in Rome, located near the Via Sacra in the Roman Forum. Built in the 7th century BC, it consists of two superimposed levels: the lower Tullianum and the upper Carcer.\r\n\r\nThroughout its history, it held notable prisoners such as Jugurtha, king of Numidia, and Vercingetorix, leader of the Gauls. According to tradition, the apostles Peter and Paul were also imprisoned here before their martyrdom.\r\n\r\nToday, the site is situated beneath the Church of San Giuseppe dei Falegnami and serves as a place of historical and religious significance.",
