    "description": "Officially added to the UNESCO World Heritage List as the 60th Italian site in 2024!\r\n\r\nThe Appian Way, once the principal highway of ancient Rome, has witnessed centuries of history. It has served as a vital trade route, a military thoroughfare, and a pilgrimage path.\r\n\r\nIts cobblestone surface, lined with ancient tombs, aqueducts, and villas, today offers a glimpse into the daily life and culture of the Romans.\r\n\r\nToday we can have some exciting experiences there: guided tours, sustainable e-golf and e-bike, bio-food and wine tastings.",
