    "description": "After a boat tour around the 3 Islands of Lake Iseo we debark on Monte Isola.\r\nMonte Isola, is one of Italy's most beautiful villages and Europe's largest lake island. Eleven towns are linked by narrow roads perfect for walking and cycling.\r\nA popular clockwise itinerary from Peschiera Maraglio follows the coast past olive groves to Sensole, then climbs to Menzino's fortress. It continues north through Sinchignano to Siviano, the \"capital,\" and offers a challenging ascent to Cure and Masse, known for salami. A twenty-minute walk from Cure leads to the Madonna della Ceriola Sanctuary, boasting breathtaking views. The loop descends to Carzano, offering views of Loreto Island, before returning to Peschiera Maraglio.",
