    "description": "Isola Bella was conceived in 1650 by Count Vitaliano VI Borromeo, who decided to transform a rock emerging from the lake into a place of delight.\r\nIt is a captivating showcase of Baroque artistry, famed for its palace adorned with intricate decorations and its breathtaking Italian gardens, a multi-tiered spectacle of fountains, statues, and vibrant flora. \r\n\r\nIn contrast, Isola Madre, the largest of the Borromean Islands, offers a more tranquil and natural experience. Its extensive botanical gardens are a haven of exotic plants, rare trees, and free-roaming birds, creating a serene and \r\npicturesque retreat.\r\n\r\n• Boat Tour and visit of the two islands",
