    "description": "Paupys market is a perfect place to meet friends of varied tastes. And for their chefs, it gives the chance to experiment and improve as the customers can give their feedback right on the spot.\r\n\r\nThere are 17 restaurants and 4 bars. It is called “market” but it is rather food court and very popular place for local people.\r\n\r\nPaupys district was mainly an industrial area. People settled here around the 17th century.  Until the beginning of the 20th century, mainly mills and workshops were built on the Vilnia River near Paupys district. They produced groats, gunpowder, paper, and flour. Paupys itself reminded more of Venice than Vilnius, with a system of canals, dams, mills, and islands.\r\n\r\nNow Paupys is the newest district in Vilnius with modern architecture; it’s right in the Old Town but surrounded by nature and tranquillity.",
