    "description": "The Treetop Walking Path is the first path in the Baltic States and entire Eastern Europe that provides an opportunity to take a walk high above the ground, at the level of treetops. \r\nThe Treetop Walking Path was opened on August 2015. The Treetop Walking Path Complex includes an information center, the path, and a watchtower.\r\n\r\nThe Treetop Walking Path is 300 meters long and gradually rises to 21 meters above the ground. \r\nThe watchtower at the end of the Path is 34 meters high and enables visitors to observe the praised Anykščiai Pinewood, admire the winding Šventoji River, and see the towers of St. Matthew Church, which is the tallest church in Lithuania.\r\n\r\nIn 2016, the Treetop Walk complex was awarded the highest rating in the category “United Nations World Tourism Organization Award for Innovation in Tourism-related Institutions”. The Treetop Walk complex was presented as a particularly successful facility that promotes ecological and cognitive tourism, contributing to sustainable development.\r\n\r\nFrom capital Vilnius to Treetop Walking is only 100 km / 1h 20 min and on located on the way to Latvia. \r\nThere are WCs, so after sightseeing it can be used as toilet stop point during long distance transfer.\r\n\r\nSome of our groups already have visited before Covid and will also visit this summer Treetop.",
    "tourProgramExample": "",
