    "tags": [
      "Animal",
      "Nature"
    ],
    "description": "Polar Park is the world's northernmost animal park, and home to Norway's large predators such as bears, wolves, and lynx as well as deer, moose, reindeer and muskox. Opened in 1994, the park is based on exhibiting animals in their natural surroundings.\r\n\r\nAnimal welfare is their greatest concern, and with this in mind the animals live in large enclosures with the liberty to hide in their natural surroundings. Most of them are however very social and curious, so the chance of observing them during your visit is high. If you are prepared to spend some time in the park it is more likely that you will get to see them all. \r\n\r\nOpened in 1994, the park is based on exhibiting animals in their natural surroundings which means that each species also gets a lot of room to romp around.\r\n\r\nWith 1100 dekar (1 dekar = 1000 square meters) in only 12 enclosures, the Polar Park is one of the animal parks in the world with the most area per animal.",
