    "tags": [],
    "description": "Seven Viking swords, dating back 1,200 years, are part of a unique exhibition at Oslo Gardermoen Airport, offering travelers a firsthand experience of the Viking Age. \r\n\r\nThe iron swords, discovered in Viking graves across Norway, including locations like Flå, Gjøvik, Nome, Nord-Aurdal, Rendalen, and Åmot, are showcased at the airport. Each sword is labeled with a number, accompanied by information on glass displays, and features a QR code linking to the museum's website for additional Viking Age exhibitions. With an expected audience of around 4 million passengers annually, the exhibition intends to promote cultural awareness in Norway. \r\n\r\nThe display will continue throughout 2025 at least.",
