    "description": "Stiklestad National Culture Centre commemorates the Battle of Stiklestad in 1030, where King Olav Haraldsson fell and later became St. Olav. The center hosts the renowned \"St. Olav Drama\" and \"Viking Summer,\" providing a vibrant festival with concerts, plays, guided tours, and a medieval market. \r\n\r\nOpen year-round, the center includes exhibitions, a museum shop, a restaurant/café, and meeting facilities. The adjacent hotel offers accommodations, and the surrounding area features historic sites such as Stiklestad Church and a folk museum with 30 buildings from the 1600-1800s.",
