    "description": "Welcome aboard!\r\n\r\nThe former Coastal Express steamer ship (1956) is on dry land, inside the modern museum building.\r\n\r\nThe ship is well maintained and ready to welcome guests all over the ship: the bridge, the galley, the engine room, the postal room, the crew department, cabins, outer decks – and more. \r\n\r\nOn the front deck there is even a Ford17M from 1971.\r\n\r\nTake in the atmosphere, see original arts and decorations on board. Enjoy food and drinks in the cafeteria anno 1956. The museum also holds a section of the former steamship DS Finmarken (1912), that also sailed as a “hurtigrute”. The sections is in incredible condition and will take you on a time travel.",
