    "tags": [],
    "description": "Lysefjord Cruise – Tranquil fjords and majestic Preikestolen \r\n\r\nStep aboard a silent, electric boat that takes you straight from the city center into the heart of serene and unspoiled fjord landscapes. After you pass Lysefjord Bridge, the gateway to the famous fjord, you are surrounded by steep and dramatic mountains. Feel the thrill when our crew steers the boat towards Fantahålå, the cave where the “vagrants” hid from the sheriff in the old days. Not long after, you will spot one of the most famous attractions in the Stavanger region – the iconic Preikestolen towering 604 meters above the fjord!  \r\n\r\nLysefjord is also home to several impressive waterfalls. To make this boat trip even more memorable, our crew brings the boat as close as possible to the thundering Hengjanefossen waterfall so you can feel the refreshing spray. \r\n\r\nIn spring and summer, they stop by friendly goats enjoying their summer in the Lysefjord mountains. With luck, you might even spot local wildlife like sea eagles, seals and porpoises!",
