    "description": "Join our bird watching trips to have the opportunity to watch white tailed eagles, gannets, puffins and other sea birds from one of our RIB boats! If you are lucky, we might also encounter harbour seals, harbor porpoises or otters.\r\n\r\nDuring the trip we stop by the island Bleiksøya, one of the most famous puffin colonies in Norway, with about 35.000 nesting puffins. We also stop at Forøy, where you will have the opportunity to see a colony of nesting gannets, guillemots, auks and cormorants.\r\n\r\nThe Puffins: During summer the puffins come closer to shore and give our guests the opportunity to experience this lovely bird. But did you know that this bird change colour in the autumn and winter? Their beak becomes black/grey and the face becomes grey.",
