    "description": "Andøya Space is Norway's only operational space center, launching sounding rockets several times a year to study space and the northern lights.\r\n\r\nAt the visitor center, Spaceship Aurora, you can explore the wonders of the northern lights, learn how they influence our planet, and discover their significance in Norwegian history and culture.\r\n\r\nJoin us in engaging activities like movies, exhibitions, virtual space missions, an escape room and more. \r\n\r\nRelease your inner explorer!\r\n\r\n*Journey to Mars* \r\nHas life ever existed on Mars? Join an exciting mission as a research crew of six traveling to the Red Planet. This interactive experience uses virtual reality technology and is perfect for adventurers of all ages, available in both English and Norwegian.\r\n\r\n*Escape 42*\r\nEarth is under attack, and only you can save it! Using logic, creativity, and teamwork, you’ll have one hour to uncover clues and solve puzzles to save the planet. This thrilling escape room is suitable for youths and adults, with a maximum of five participants per group.",
