    "description": "ABOUT ACTIVITY\r\nEmbark on an 43 km unforgettable \r\njourney along Norway’s northernmost \r\nOfoten railway, where you’ll travel \r\nthrough breathtaking Arctic landscapes \r\nwith panoramic views of mountains and \r\nfjords aboard the “Arctic Train.” \r\nStarting at the Narvik train station, \r\nwe’ll take you on a round trip traveling \r\nfrom Narvik to the Swedish border \r\nat Bjørnfjell and back with stops at \r\nscenic stations along the journey. \r\nEnjoy stunning sights of the ice-blue \r\nfjord, mountains, and waterfalls while \r\nyour onboard guide shares fascinating \r\nhistorical facts.\r\nINCLUDED\r\n• Roundtrip train ticket: Narvik – \r\nBjørnfjell – Narvik.\r\n• Audioguide and free Wi-Fi.\r\n• Onboard host serving complimentary \r\ncoffee and tea.\r\n• 10–15 minute station stops where \r\nguests can step off the train.\r\nGOOD TO KNOW\r\n• The train slows down at select spots \r\nfor photo opportunities.\r\n• The route runs between Narvik and \r\nBjørnfjell, the final stop before the \r\nSwedish border.\r\n• Private charters are available.\r\n• Maximum capacity: 440 people, with \r\n360 window seats",
