    "description": "ABOUT ACTIVITY\r\nJoin us on this unique journey as we  travel along the historic Ofoten Railway, away from city light pollution. This isn’t just any ride - it’s a unique quest into the Arctic night, chasing one of nature’s most spectacular phenomena, the Aurora Borealis. Surrounded by dark  night skies, we will have great chances of witnessing the northern lights!\r\n\r\nOur first stop is at the Swedish bordertown, Bjørnfjell station. After a short stop, we will continue our journey \r\nto Katterat station, located 373 meters above sea level. At Katterat station, we’ll step off the train to immerse ourselves in the Arctic night, gathering around a cozy campfire under the open sky.\r\n\r\nYour guide will serve hot drinks and a fresh pastry as we wait for the northern lights to appear, adding warmth and comfort to this magical moment.\r\n\r\nAfterward, we’ll return to the train and journey back to Narvik, hopefully bringing with you magical memories and images of this unforgettable experience. \r\nINCLUDED\r\n• Train ticket \r\n• Snack, beverages and bonfire \r\n• Guide and photo tips\r\n• Northern Lights documentary movie\r\n• Visit the mountain village of Katterat \r\nand the museum at the old barrack \r\n\r\nGOOD TO KNOW\r\n• Bring warm clothes \r\n• Camera and Tripod (optional)\r\n• Maximum capacity: 440 people, with \r\n360 window seats.",
