    "description": "The Reindeer Feeding & Sami Culture experience is an immersive Arctic activity that brings you close to the heart of Sámi traditions and their long-standing relationship with reindeer.\r\n\r\nAfter a short scenic transfer from Tromsø, you’ll visit a reindeer camp where you can hand-feed and interact with a friendly herd of reindeer — an unforgettable chance to connect with these iconic Arctic animals as they roam the snowy landscape.\r\n\r\nIncluded in the experience is time spent in a traditional lavvu (Sámi tent) or similar shelter, where you’ll enjoy warm drinks and a hearty, traditional meal such as bidos (a Sámi reindeer stew), alongside stories and insights shared by local Sámi guides. As you eat and relax by the fire, you’ll learn about Sámi history, culture and reindeer herding traditions, and have the chance to hear traditional joik songs — an important part of Sámi cultural expression.\r\n\r\nThis family-friendly outing offers a meaningful introduction to the Sámi way of life, blending nature, food, storytelling and cultural heritage into a memorable Arctic adventure that’s suitable for all ages.",
