    "description": "A RIB Safari with Viking Adventure is a thrilling 2-hour coastal excursion that blends speed, scenery, nature and local culture around Haugesund. After meeting your guide at the cruise terminal (or designated pier) you’ll be equipped with a safety suit, life jacket, goggles and gloves, and given a brief run-through of what to expect. \r\n\r\nOnce aboard the rigid inflatable boat, your experienced local captain will navigate through the scenic straits and channels that thread between islands off the coast — waters steeped in history, including the fjord routes that helped shape early Norway’s seafaring heritage. The RIB picks up speed out toward the open sea, giving you moments of high-adrenaline riding, sea spray, and wide views across rugged archipelagos. \r\n\r\nAlong the way you’ll hear stories about the area’s maritime past and island life, with opportunities to appreciate the rocky shores, sheltered bays and local wildlife — including, if you’re lucky, a glance of a white-tailed eagle near its nesting grounds. It’s an experience that combines the excitement of a high-speed boat ride with genuine insight into Norway’s coastal culture and scenery, ideal for adventurous visitors who want more than just a sightseeing cruise.",
