    "description": "Your visit begins with time spent among the reindeer, where you can feed them, take pictures, and learn about their way of living in the Arctic. Afterwards, we invite you into our warm lávvu (a traditional Sámi tent). Here, around the open fire, you’ll enjoy coffee or tea while we share stories about life in the north, Sámi culture, and the challenges and traditions that shape it today.\r\n\r\nWith VisitReindeer, you don’t just see reindeer—you step into their world. Surrounded by mountains and, if you’re lucky, the northern lights, you’ll experience nature and culture in harmony, the way it has been lived for generations.\r\n\r\nThis tour includes:\r\n- Reindeer encounter and feeding\r\n- Storytelling and cultural insight with your Sámi host\r\n- Coffee or tea served in the lávvu by the fire\r\n\r\nGroup size: Small groups for a personal experience\r\n\r\nWhat to bring: Warm outdoor clothing and sturdy shoes. Arctic weather can change quickly!\r\n\r\nGood to know: This is a family-friendly activity, suitable for all ages.",
