    "description": "The Himakånå guided tour is a 5-hour outdoor experience that takes you to one of the region’s most scenic viewpoints, often called the “Mini Trolltunga.”\r\n\r\nThe tour starts from Haugesund city center where you drive to the village of Nedstrand and pick up a traditional Norwegian packed lunch (“matpakke”) before the hike begins.\r\n\r\nFrom Nedstrand you hike roughly 2.2 km up a steep gravel road to the top of Himakånå, which sits about 357 m above sea level. The walk takes about an hour each way and offers beautiful views along the trail. At the summit you can rest, enjoy your lunch and take in panoramic fjord views, a popular photo spot.\r\n\r\nThe tour includes transport, an English-speaking guide, lunch, bottled water and a small backpack. Guides adapt the pace to the group’s fitness level, and the hike is suitable for people in good physical shape.\r\n\r\nClothing and shoes suitable for weather and hiking are recommended. The meeting time is generally at least 10 minutes before departure at the cruise tererminal",
