    "description": "Visitors wander underground around the Cloth Hall on glass ramps and footbridges suspended above preserved medieval routes, the oldest of which date back to the 11th century.\r\n\r\nThe permanent exhibition includes:\r\n- former waterworks\r\n- crossroads of road routes\r\n- pre-foundation settlement\r\n- Bolesławowe Stalls\r\n- Bogeous Stalls\r\n- Krakow's main export goods\r\n- medieval pavements of the Cloth Hall\r\n- map of distant trade\r\n- reconstruction of twelfth-century goldsmith and blacksmith workshops\r\n- relics of a burnt settlement\r\n- model of the fifteenth-century city\r\n- 11th-century cemetery\r\n- historiography of the city of Krakow\r\n- holograms\r\n- development of the Market Square\r\n- reconstruction of a medieval merchant's stall\r\n- projection rooms and a cinema hall\r\n- children's zone but often visited also by adults because of the theatre in which you can watch legends of Old Krakow.",
