    "description": "When was the last time you ate at the bottom of the sea?\r\n\r\nTreat a lucky soul to a special dinner in the Orientarium Zoo's underwater tunnel. Experience a culinary adventure combined with an amazing spectacle unfolding before your eyes. Look around carefully and raise your head as thousands of exotic fish swim around you. Among the 180 species of marine fauna gathered in Orientarium (Lodz city) you will be able to spot bowmouth guitarfish, bearded sharks, giant gurams, blacktip and brown sharks, spotted eagle rays and great barracudas.\r\n\r\nThe venue is arranged in an underwater tunnel of Zoo (Lodz city) and has capacity for around 40 persons. The room temperature is around 25°C. Oceanic zone as a whole has capacity up to 150 persons (sitting).\r\n \r\nThere is on-site conference center for up to 500 persons with 6 different sizes of conference rooms (1000m2 of multifunctional event space) which can be used for conference before dinner.",
