    "description": "Riese (Giant) is the code name for a construction project of Nazi Germany in 1943-1945, consisting of seven underground structures located in the Owl Mountains (Gory Sowie) in Poland.\r\nIt can be easily reached from Wroclaw (ca. 1 hour drive, 75 km).\r\n\r\nWorld War II. From 1943, the Germans were undertaking large-scale construction works known as the Project Riese in the region of the Owl Mountains. The construction was never finished and what remains today is a number of constructions, the purpose of which is still uncertain. \r\nThe Drifts are more than 500 meters long, with the capacity of 14 000 m3. The Structure consists of three parallel tunnels. \r\nA tourist route is enriched with audio-visual effects.\r\nIn the decades following the WWII, only few daredevils could admire the enormous work, which had been done in drilling the kilometers of tunnels in solid rock and which had cost the lives of thousands of people.\r\nToday, it is a safe and easily accessible tourist attraction. We invite you to visit one of the most interesting and most mysterious military places in the Owl Mountains.\r\n \r\nThe complex is located on a borderline between the villages of Rzeczka and Walim. \r\nIt can be easily reached from Wroclaw (ca. 1 hour drive, 75 km).",
    "tourProgramExample": "",
    "officialWebsite": "https://sztolnie.pl/en/gallery/",
    "capacityMin": 0,
    "capacityMax": 150,
    "capacityDetails": "The tour lasts about 60 minutes at a temperature of 5-10 degrees with 90% humidity in groups of about 50 people. Up to 150 people can stay in the tunnels at the same time.",
    "priceMin": 0,
