    "tags": [
      "Team building",
      "Workshop",
      "Traditional"
    ],
    "description": "Painting of a relief tile, suitable for ceramic initiation.\r\n\r\nIn this type of workshop for groups we find the Hispano-Moorish tiles, painted with the arista technique, more interesting, since the results are always very stimulating and when ready they become a beautiful piece to keep.\r\n\r\nThe tiles have hand-carved relief and the same stands out with the painting.\r\n\r\nThe tiles are produced manually, through artisanal processes in our workshop and the activity also demonstrates the manufacturing process. \r\n\r\nDon't worry, no artistic skills are required :)\r\n\r\nAt the end of the workshop, the tiles are baked in our kiln and the delivery time is at least 48 hours. \r\n\r\nThere are no ceramic kilns that can fire to deliver the tiles on the same day, because glazes take hours to fuse.\r\n\r\nOur suggestion is that you plan this activity for the first day you're in Porto, so that we have time to bake the tiles and you can pick them up at the workshop before you leave. \r\n\r\n👉 We will have Port wine to accompany the activity. :)\r\nThey could be painting and drinking Port Wine.\r\nWe also offer still water, coffee and soft drinks.",
    "tourProgramExample": "",
    "officialWebsite": "https://agostinha.com/",
