    "description": "One of the loveliest picturesque old, and best-preserved historical town along the Adriatic coast, is a gem of Venetian Gothic architecture. The town has much medieval architecture, with narrow streets and compact houses .\r\n\r\nPiran is the birthplace of the composer and violinist Giuseppe Tartini, who played an important role in shaping its cultural heritage. \r\n\r\nImportant Sightseeing spots are: \r\nCathedral of Saint George, port Piran, Piran Town hall, Piran wall,  Maritime museum, the Cloisters of Saint Francis Monastery and the Museum of Underwater Activities.\r\n\r\nSightseeing tour in Piran takes 1,5h (usually is combined with SS tour of Portoroz)",
