    "description": "Guerila, a biodynamic wine-growing farm in the village of Planina near Ajdovscina in the Vipava valley has been established in 2005.\r\n\r\nThe offer is interestingly divided into three lines:\r\n\r\n1. Guerila classic is the newest batch of wines that, following a short maceration, ripen in stainless steel containers. They preserve their characteristic varietal aroma and taste. They are designed for relaxed enjoyment on every occasion. \r\n\r\n2. Guerila selection includes wines with prolonged maceration, ripened in traditional wooden barrels. They combine elegance, drinkability and sophistication.\r\n\r\n3. Guerila extreme are wines of selected vintages that, after prolonged maceration, ferment in traditional barrels or clay amphorae. They are only bottled after a couple of years and are distinguished by harmony and exceptional complexity.",
