    "description": "Its catamarans offer the possibility of an unforgettable Mussel Route along the Ria de Arousa, of approximately 1 hour duration, departing from the Port of O Grove or from the Island of La Toja.\r\n\r\nWhile sailing, you will see the importance of fishing, shellfishing and aquaculture in the Ria de Arousa, the largest and most productive of Galicia.\r\n\r\nYou will visit the mussel, oyster and scallop farms, while the boats fish. You will make a stop to observe, through the underwater vision glasses, the bottom of the sea and the fish that live under the farms.\r\n\r\nFrom the boat you will see the shellfish banks, islets such as \"A Figueira\", where the Tower of San Sadurniño is located, an ancient medieval fortress; the island of Arousa and its natural reserve of Punta Carreirón; villages such as Cambados, capital of Albariño wine; and O Grove, a town of tourist excellence and its inshore port.\r\n\r\nDuring the crossing you will taste steamed mussels from the estuary on board the ship, accompanied with water, wine or soft drinks.",
