    "description": "Guided 4x4 or trailer tour + a glass of wine, beer, or soft drink and a charcuterie board.\r\nApproximate duration: 2-3 hours.\r\nGuided tour of the most important enclosures of the bull breeding farm, livestock facilities, tienta ring, and horse stable.\r\n€35 per person.\r\n\r\nExtras:\r\nTo the visit price, extras chosen should be added.\r\n\r\n*** Bullfighting Class in the tienta ring of the bull breeding farm.\r\nApproximate duration: 1 hour.\r\nWith a professional from our team: €200.\r\nWith a novillero or matador: €350.\r\nWith matador \"Víctor Puerto\": €600.\r\nWith a current well-known matador (subject to availability): from €1500 to 4.000.\r\n\r\n*** Aperitif at the bull breeding farm (Water, beer, wine, soft drinks, potato chips, olives, charcuterie, cheese, and Spanish omelette).\r\n€25 per person.\r\n\r\n*** Aperitif (as above) and Lunch (Salad, country-style chickpea stew, seasonal fruit or homemade dessert. Water, beer, wine, and soft drinks).\r\n€40 per person.\r\n\r\n*** Witness a professional Tentadero with 2 cows.\r\n€1.500 per group. This involves having contact with a real bullfighter, who would explain the aspects of the tentadero, alongside the rancher.\r\n\r\nOTHER EXTRAS:\r\n\r\n*** Ham cutter and tasting of \"Juan Pedro Domecq\" Iberian products. From €1500 according to the piece (cutter and piece).\r\n*** Spanish guitar. From €350 according to the artist. Something simple and integrated into the estate and atmosphere.\r\n*** Specific chef – costs for the menu and their fees would need to be assessed.",
