    "description": "In the first part of the proposed visit, lasting approximately 60 minutes, a local guide will accompany you along the entire trail that winds through the pasture until reaching the place where Iberian pigs roam freely. The guide will provide a detailed interpretation of the path, highlighting the flora and fauna that can be encountered.\r\n\r\nThe journey begins at Marimateo rest area, the source of the Odiel River, a 5-minute drive from the town of Aracena.\r\n\r\nIn this second part, also lasting approximately 60 minutes, we will tour the different rooms of our ham and sausage factory, including the natural curing room for hams and shoulders located on the top floor. You will witness the artisanal process of making our pork-derived products and learn about the curing process of our hams and shoulders.\r\n\r\nThe visit concludes with a tasting of our finest cured products, such as acorn-fed Iberian ham, accompanied by a good glass of \"Marqués de Aracena\" wine. While enjoying the tasting, you can explore the public retail store located within the same factory, where you can purchase any of our products.",
