    "description": "Petritegi had a wooden wine press to make cider with the apples on his property. The cider produced was intended for family consumption, but was also marketed to supply the Guipuzcoan fishing fleet, for sale to individuals and for consumption in the so-called \"cider taverns\" or cider houses.\r\n\r\nCurrently, the Petritegi cider house is an ideal place to taste cider and Basque gastronomy: surrounded by nature and apple trees, plus it's just 5 km away from San Sebastián.",
    "tourProgramExample": "*Txotx experience:\r\nshort visit of 20/25 minutes where after an introduction, we watch a video about the production and go to the winery to make a txotx (drink cider from the barrels). \r\n\r\n*Gastronomy experience:\r\n1h10 minute visit where after the introduction, we watch the video about the production, we go to the apple trees, we see the old press, production area and wineries. During this tour we taste 4 different products.\r\n\r\n*Make your own cider:\r\na 1-hour activity where after the introduction, attendees go to the apple trees to pick apples, transport the apple to the production area the old-fashioned way, wash and break the apple and press it to obtain apple juice . We finish by making a txotx.",
