    "description": "The route from La Rambleta to the Pico del Teide is relatively short but quite challenging due to the altitude. The trail starts at La Rambleta, which is located at 3,555 meters above sea level, right where the cable car arrives, and ascends towards the crater of the volcano, reaching 3,718 meters at the summit.\r\n\r\nFrom the top, you’ll have an incredible view of Tenerife, and if the day is clear, you can even see other islands in the archipelago.\r\n\r\nThis route requires a special permit to access the summit, as there are restrictions in place to protect the natural area. The trail is well-marked, but you should be prepared for the physical effort required to hike at high altitudes.\r\n\r\nThe route is in Tenerife\r\nDistance: Approximately 650 meters (one way).\r\nElevation Gain: About 163 meters of ascent.\r\nStarting Point: La Rambleta (3,555 m).\r\nEnding Point: Pico del Teide (3,718 m).",
