    "description": "Garajonay National Park - Route from Laguna Grande to Alto de Garajonay, La Gomera\r\n\r\nThe Laguna Grande to Alto de Garajonay route is one of the most iconic trails in Garajonay National Park, known for its dense laurel forests, misty atmosphere, and stunning viewpoints.\r\n\r\nStarting from Laguna Grande, a popular recreational area, the trail gradually ascends through lush vegetation to the Alto de Garajonay, the highest point on La Gomera at 1,487 meters. From the summit, you can enjoy panoramic views of the island and, on clear days, even spot other islands like Tenerife, La Palma, and El Hierro.\r\n\r\nThe park is a UNESCO World Heritage site due to its unique ecosystems and rich biodiversity, making this route an exceptional nature experience.\r\n\r\nDistance: Approximately 5 km (one way).\r\nElevation Gain: About 300 meters of ascent.\r\nStarting Point: Laguna Grande.\r\nEnding Point: Alto de Garajonay.\r\nPoints of Interest: Dense laurel forests, endemic flora and fauna, panoramic views from the summit.",
