    "tags": [],
    "description": "A tour in the campo bravo offer an immersion in the amazing world of the Toro Bravo, the fighting bull, in the deepest of the andalucian culture, nearby Sevilla.\r\n\r\n\"We are bullfighting professionals: matadors de toros, picadors, riders and culture enthusiasts. We don't recite a lesson, but share with you our present, our past and our hopes.\r\n\r\nIn over ten years of professional activity, we have welcomed and accompanied travellers and professionals, on individual visits or company conventions for more than 250 people.\r\n\r\nThis is not an exotic visit, but a profound experience, an immersion in the daily life of the toro people. It's a direct encounter with our world, an essential part of Andalusian culture.\r\n\r\nWe can receive you directly in French (native), Spanish or English (fluent).\"\r\n\r\nPlease consult attached dossier.",
    "tourProgramExample": "- Arrival at the farm at the agreed time.\r\n- Welcome coffee.\r\n- Introduction in the courtyard of the farm.\r\n- In the hall of the bullfighting museum, a brief history of bullfighting and cattle raising (why bulls are played with, which we see in the ring, and why they are bred).\r\n- In the bullfighters' museum, the development of a bullfight is explained (its protocol and the meaning of this spectacle)\r\n- Walk through the Dehesa in a 4x4, where you will see the cows, the young bulls and the bulls.\r\n- Aperitif in the Dehesa, close to the cows, (in case of rain, it will be given at the end of the visit in the hall, veranda or museum).\r\n- Visit to the bullfighting ring and the corrals, where it is possible to receive a bullfighting lesson from a matador or a young bullfighter (optional).\r\n- Visit to the stables.",
