    "description": "Cruise on the Guadalquivir River, a hop-on hop-off bus tour, and more excursions to enjoy sightseeing in Seville.\r\nBoat rental for events available. \r\n\r\n\r\nThe pier located in front of the Torre del Oro in Marqués de Contadero is the departure point for this exciting cruise along the Guadalquivir, Seville's river.\r\n\r\nDuring the boat trip through Seville, you'll be able to admire some of its most notable monuments, such as the San Telmo Palace, the seat of the presidency of the Andalusian Regional Government, the majestic Maestranza Theater, and the beautiful Cristina Gardens, among others.\r\n\r\nYou'll also have the opportunity to see the main pavilions and monuments of the 1929 Ibero-American Exposition and Cartuja Island, the site of Expo 92. During this part of the tour, you'll see the modern Navigation Pavilion and the imposing Sevilla Tower, the city's first large skyscraper.\r\n\r\nBefore returning to the starting point at the Torre del Oro pier, you'll have the opportunity to see one of Seville's most historic sites: the docks where Christopher Columbus, Juan Sebastián Elcano, and Magellan departed.\r\n\r\nThe approximate duration of the Seville cruise is one hour, and it is an unforgettable experience for those who wish to discover the beauty and cultural richness of the city from a unique perspective and with all the comforts.",
