    "description": "A Creative Madrid Discovered Door to Door\r\n\r\nThe “Made in Madrid” experience is curated and guided by Heather Evans, originally from the United States and a resident of Madrid for nearly two decades.\r\n\r\nDuring a journey of more than three hours through Madrid’s Salamanca District, guests discover a unique expression of luxury through craftsmanship, design, and local savoir-faire.\r\n\r\nThroughout the tour, encounters with creators, shared stories, and the leisurely pace of the experience create an authentic immersion into Madrid’s vibrant creative scene.",
    "tourProgramExample": "1. Visit La Pajarita, Madrid’s historic chocolatier established in 1852, and enjoy a tasting experience introducing the city’s heritage and traditional flavors.\r\n\r\n2. Explore the atelier and boutique of Ágatha Ruiz de la Prada, showcasing the designer’s distinctive and avant-garde creations.\r\n\r\n3. Visit the workshop of Mimoki and discover handcrafted haute couture headwear and accessories combining tradition and contemporary design.\r\n\r\n4. Continue to Redondo Brand and experience the world of one of Spain’s leading emerging fashion designers.\r\n\r\n5. Enjoy a refreshment break at La Anxoita.\r\n\r\n6. Visit the atelier of Suma Cruz and discover handcrafted jewelry inspired by nature, culture, and imagination.\r\n\r\n7. Conclude at Casa LOEWE, where fashion, contemporary art, and architecture come together in the flagship store of the historic Spanish luxury house.",
