    "description": "The Fort de Chillon museum is the ideal place for an immersive, intergenerational visit. Located in a former Swiss army bunker, classified as a defense secret until 2001, the Fort de Chillon museum guarantees a successful outing whatever the weather, sun or rain, thanks to its constant temperature.\r\n\r\nA 2'125 m2 Super-Forteresse hidden oppostie side of Chillon Castle in a spectacular landscape between the shores of Lake Geneva in Montreux and the mountains of the Vaud Alps.\r\n\r\nAn ideal place for adventure-seekers, families in search of entertainment or simply for those curious to discover one of the Swiss army's best-kept secrets. In short, a unique visit in Switzerland, just 30 minutes from Lausanne, 45 minutes from Evian-les-Bains and an hour from Bern and Geneva.",
