    "description": "Bechtel Winery is a boutique Swiss winery located on the sunny slopes above the Rhine, in a region with over 1,000 years of winemaking tradition.\r\n\r\nRun by winemaker Mathias Bechtel, the estate produces high-quality wines with a strong focus on sustainability and respect for nature. Guests can enjoy authentic wine tastings in a charming setting, discover local varieties that reflect the unique terroir of Eglisau, and take part in a guided vineyard hike with educational insights into soil, terroir, and biodiversity.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Classic Tasting:\r\nWINES TASTING w BREAD STICK/Chips (4 Wines), CELLAR VISIT, Duration: approx. 1.5 hours\r\n\r\nShort Hike in Vineyards before tasting w educational input on Soil. Terroir, Biodiversity, Duration: approx.. 30 min\r\n\r\nPossibility to add Charcuterie Board (Meats, Cheese), Bread or but a Wine bottle as souvenir for a special rate!\r\n\r\nto book:\r\n1. only activity at Winery Bechtel (guest arrive by themself)\r\n2. Trip from and back to Zurich with private transfer\r\n3. Guests taking train by themself and have horse carriage to the Winery and the nature (1hour)",
