    "description": "Lafcadio Hearn Japanese Gardens in Tramore, County Waterford, is a serene, 2.5-acre tribute to the life and global travels of writer Lafcadio Hearn (Koizumi Yakumo).\r\n\r\nFeaturing 11 symbolic garden “rooms” tracing his journey—from Victorian youth to his love for Japan—the gardens include authentic elements like a tea house, red bridge, wisteria frame, ponds, and rock formations.\r\n\r\nWith audio guides, family-friendly trails, and a hillside view over Tramore Bay, the gardens offer a peaceful, cross-cultural experience celebrating Irish-Japanese heritage and Hearn’s storytelling legacy.",
