    "description": "Brownlow House, also known as Brownlow Castle, is a magnificent 19th-century mansion located in Lurgan, County Armagh. Built in 1833 for the 1st Baron Lurgan, this striking Elizabethan-style estate has played a key role in Irish and wartime history—serving as military headquarters during both World Wars, including a visit from General Eisenhower.\r\n\r\nToday, Brownlow House offers visitors a unique experience through its award-winning World War exhibitions, housed in atmospheric basement galleries filled with original artifacts and soldier graffiti. Set beside the scenic Lurgan Park, it’s a wonderful place to explore Northern Ireland’s heritage and take in beautiful surroundings.\r\n\r\nGuests can enjoy guided tours of the house and gardens, and round off their visit with traditional afternoon tea or a hearty Sunday roast, available for lunch or dinner.",
