    "description": "Brook Hall Estate and Gardens is a private 18th-century demesne recognised for its historical significance and pioneering approach to environmental sustainability. Owned by the Gilliland family since 1856, the estate is home to one of the premier private arboretums in Northwest Ireland and is the first farm in Northern Ireland to be measurably carbon-positive. The estate has opened its doors to the public and offer a range of expeirences to suit almost everyones interests, including: Garden tour of the Arboretum, Sunstainability tours, afternoon tea packages, artistic workshops, history walks, dining experiences, cycling and horseback tours and cocktail masterclasses - to name a few.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Through the Garden Gates Garden Tour & Afternoon Tea\r\n\r\nDiscover the beauty of one of the finest arboretums in Northwest Ireland as you're guided through the gardens, before arriving for afternoon tea in the stunning walled garden on the banks of the river. (1.5 hr walking / 1.5 hr afternoon tea)",
