    "description": "Hidden London is London Transport Museum’s exclusive programme of tours at disused stations and secret sites across London. Led by expert guides, ready to share unusual and little-known stories surrounding the stations’ varied histories, these visits offer an exciting opportunity to explore locations rarely seen by the public.\r\n\r\nCheck out some iconic lines like:\r\n\r\nAldwych: The End of the Line\r\nThis iconic \"ghost station\" closed in 1994. Discover its transition from Blitz shelter to a premier filming location for hits like  Darkest Hour, The ABC Murders, Sherlock, and Atonement.\r\n\r\nBaker Street: The World’s First Underground\r\nStep back to 1863 to see where the steam-powered revolution began. Access original platforms and corridors hidden from the public for over seventy-five years.\r\n\r\nCharing Cross: Behind the Silver Screen\r\nGo behind closed doors to the disused Jubilee line platforms. Walk under Trafalgar Square and see the cinematic backdrop for blockbusters like Skyfall and Thor.\r\n\r\nClapham South: Subterranean Shelter\r\nJourney eleven stories underground into a deep-level shelter. Hear moving stories of WWII Londoners and Caribbean migrants who once sought refuge in these vast tunnels.",
    "tourProgramExample": "",
    "officialWebsite": "https://www.ltmuseum.co.uk/hidden-london",
