    "tags": [],
    "description": "Located just one hour south of Edinburgh in the Scottish Borders, the Great Tapestry of Scotland offers a distinctive, story-led cultural experience that is easy to integrate into a wide range of itineraries.\r\n\r\nThrough 160 hand-embroidered panels, the Tapestry brings Scotland’s history to life in a highly visual and engaging way. In particular, their guided experience upgrade option has proven to work very well for both touring groups and specialist interest visitors, ensuring clarity, depth and a memorable visit.\r\n\r\nEach experience invites guests to slow down, connect\r\nwith Scotland’s stories, and create a meaningful,\r\nhandmade artwork inspired by the Great Tapestry of\r\nScotland — a creative, hands-on cultural experience\r\nwhere they don’t just view Scotland’s story, they make a\r\npiece of it to take home. All experiences include time to explore the exhibition.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Threads of Scotland: Wet Felting Inspired by Wool and Landscape\r\n\r\nUsing traditional wet felting techniques, visitors\r\nwork with local wool to create a tactile artwork\r\ninspired by Scotland’s land, animals, and textile\r\nheritage. For example, a felted landscape evoking\r\nhills and skies, a sheep or animal form, or an\r\nabstract felt panel echoing the colours and\r\ntextures of the Tapestry.",
    "officialWebsite": "https://www.greattapestryofscotland.com/",
