    "description": "Guests are encouraged to connect with one of the world’s greatest art collections with the launch of the National Gallery’s brand-new Sketch Tours, available from 8 June 2026.\r\n \r\nJourney through art history and explore your own creativity on this expertly guided sketch tour. Guests will learn the basics of sketching and perspective, all whilst gaining a deeper understanding of influential artworks and the artists that created them. \r\n \r\nWhether they are a complete beginner or a seasoned sketcher, these immersive experiences invite them to see the collection in an entirely new way. All art materials are provided.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Sketch Private Daytime Tour\r\nEnjoy a private 90-minute sketch experience during gallery opening hours, with the freedom to continue exploring the collection before or after your tour. Available daily between 10:00am and 4:00pm, lasting 1.5 hours.\r\n\r\nSketch Out of Hours Tour\r\nTaking place before or after public opening hours, this intimate experience allows you to escape the crowds as you enjoy sketching some of the world’s most known artworks in tranquillity. Available daily before opening 9 am–10am and after closure 6pm–7pm, lasting 1 hour. \r\n\r\nGuests can further elevate the experience with the option of a private breakfast or champagne and canapés.\r\n\r\nTours are conducted in English, with Italian, French, Spanish, and German available upon request for an additional fee.",
