    "description": "During this out of hours tour groups can explore the heritage building and escape the crowds. Led by an expert guide, these tours provide exclusive access to remarkable collections and historic buildings within the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Maritime Greenwich.\r\n\r\nQueens House is Britain's first classical building, the Queen's House, was once a royal retreat and is now home to an outstanding collection of art. With exclusive access and the expertise of a dedicated guide, guests can discover the stories behind celebrated works including Elizabeth I's Armada Portrait and the magnificent Solebay Tapestry, while enjoying the tranquillity of one of Britain's most important historic buildings before or after public opening hours.",
