    "description": "Step aboard the iconic Cutty Sark for an exclusive out-of-hours experience aboard the world's only surviving tea clipper. Discover the remarkable story of this legendary ship, celebrated for its record-breaking voyages and pioneering design that transformed global trade. With the guidance of an expert, explore the beautifully preserved decks and gain fascinating insights into the daily lives of the sailors who crossed the world's oceans. \r\n\r\nHighlights include standing beneath the ship's impressive copper-clad hull in the dry berth and admiring the world's largest collection of ship figureheads. This intimate after-hours tour offers a unique perspective on one of Britain's greatest maritime treasures.",
