    "description": "In Denmark, the merger of municipalities that began in 2004 reduced the number of municipalities from 14 counties to 5 regions and 271 municipalities to 98. The purpose of this merger was to expand the size of a single municipality to a population of 30,000 or more, and to improve the efficiency and improvement of administrative services by transferring prefectural operations. \r\n\r\nThe city of Svenborg was awarded \"Best City of the Year\" in 2000 for its innovative municipal management and advanced welfare policies in Denmark. \r\n\r\nSvenborg City:\r\nIt is a municipality with a population of about 60,000 located in the southern part of Funen Island.\r\nAs well as being a thriving commercial town, Svenborg and the surrounding islands are known for their unique nature and sea beauty, making them a popular tourist destination.\r\nIt is also a city with one of the largest high schools in Denmark, vocational schools with various courses, seafarer training schools, and a well-developed education system.\r\n\r\nIn recent years, we have also been focusing on accepting inspections, including welfare for the elderly, child welfare, welfare for the disabled, the environment, energy, and urban planning.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Due to organizational changes, Svendborg City Hall is not currently offering the following inspection programs.\r\n\r\nFuture visits to Svenborg will be individual facilities depending on the request. (I don't think it's impossible to make a referral to Svenborg City Hall, but I think it will take some time to get information because there is no tariff or list of places to visit as in the past.) ）\r\n\r\n-----------------------------------\r\n\r\nHalf Day Program\r\n-Meet and greet by a representative\r\n-Lectures by city officials\r\n　(Administrative Reform and Municipal Mergers)\r\n-Policies to improve the city's brand power\r\n- Lunch at a local restaurant with city politicians\r\n\r\nExample of the hearing when arranged in TTAO25359'08 (about 2 hours):\r\n-Environmental Policy\r\n-Strengthening the brand power of Svendborg, incorporating creative youth, ecotourism and health tourism\r\n-Environmental education for children\r\n-Municipal administration after municipal merger\r\n-Management of social welfare\r\n\r\nIn the above content, it was DKR 1750 per group + DKR 100 per person.",
    "officialWebsite": "http://www.svendborg.dk/",
