    "tags": [
      "Sustainability"
    ],
    "description": "T/V  Sustainablity progrmme by HOK-Elanto/S group, to be organised at Prisma Kaari supermarket.\r\n\r\nAs of 2024, the programme available exclusively for Kuoni Tumlare groups (incl all markets and tour types)\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------\r\nVisit at local store - How is the \r\nsustainablity programme visible at the store?\r\n\r\nWhole S-group has been carrying out systematic corporate responsibility work in all areas of operations already for many years. During the visit, the main focus is at the sustainability actions made in one of our stores, Prisma Kaari Kannelmäki. \r\n\r\nVisit details:\r\nThe visit is led by the store manager or sustainablity director, at the store of Prisma Karri Kannelmäki.\r\nDuring the visit, you will explore the operation and methods at the store by visiting different store sections and facilities. \r\n\r\nFor details, please refer to the attached PDF.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Tour programme will be discussed on request basis, depends on the clients' interests. \r\n\r\n----------------------------\r\nDuring this visit you will be demonstrated how different goals of the sustainability programme are visible:\r\n• in store’s daily operation\r\n• to the customers\r\n\r\nChosen sustainability themes can be discussed with the supplier for other topics if requested.\r\n\r\nFor example: \r\n• Environmentally friendly food / local food - How are the\r\nseason’s vegetables presented in vegetables section,\r\n- What steps have been taken to increase the portion of fish in the shopping basket? - Vegetarian options\r\n• Reduction of food waste in different product groups -\r\nHow can the store decrease the amount of food waste\r\n• How is the amount of waste decreased at the store (and\r\nin the product chain) - What types of recyclable waste are\r\ngenerated at the store, how is the waste collected and what is the current recycling rate, and how can it be improved?\r\n• Supporting equality and human rights at the store\r\n• Presentation of S-Mobiili App - Helpful tools for\r\nsustainable consumption (customers), - My Purchases\r\nservice; customers’ own purchases from the store\r\n• Customers’ carbon neutral arrival to the store - bicycles,\r\npublic transportation, electric car charging points etc.\r\n• How to make recycling easy for the customers as part\r\nof their visit to the store - What types of recyclable waste\r\nare accepted at the store, and how much waste is gathered through these collection points?",
