    "description": "Kierrätyskeskus is the Helsinki Metropolitan Area Reuse Centre, which is an excellent destionation for those who are interested in sustainable development and circular economy. \r\n\r\nA visit to the biggest reuse centre in Finland is a guided tour in the faciliites that cover an area of about 1500 square meters. \r\nVisitors have the opportunity to see the backstage of the operations from the donation point through sorting and pricing departments to different workshops and eventually the journey of discovery arrives to one of their largest secondhand stores.\r\n\r\nThe tour would be guided by their environmental eductators who have decades of experiences in sustainability education. During the visit, viritosr get to touch, sense, experiment, ask question and learn.",
