    "description": "The largest farmers' union in France, founded in 1946. It has 36 professional associations, more than 20,000 local agricultural cooperatives, and more than 600,000 farmers. It is a member of the COPA (EU Federation of Agricultural Organizations) and IFAP (International Federation of Agricultural Producers), and in 2003 expressed solidarity at the February 15 WTO International Citizens' Meeting. In 2007, the president of FNSEA was the president of COPA (EU Federation of Agricultural Organizations).\r\n\r\n*Not accepted until the end of 2015. It is undecided when it will be accepted again after that*\r\n（as of 30JUL2015)",
    "tourProgramExample": "Further reading: National Federation of Agricultural Cooperatives\r\nWTO Glossary (6th edition, October 2007)\r\nAppendix 8 Major Overseas Agricultural Organizations\r\nhttp://www.zenchu-ja.or.jp/food/wto/wtokanrenyougo/170.html\r\n・Appendix 1 Major English abbreviations and Japanese comparison table\r\nhttp://www.zenchu-ja.or.jp/food/wto/wtokanrenyougo/163.html\r\n\r\n=======================================\r\n\r\nTTAO231006-06JUL18 NOKA05 A)CTS IWA SORACHI JA LON/PAR 8 (GRQ TYO-1553) 18+1\r\n*Inquiries only 18.05.09 \r\n\r\nDesired date and time: Tuesday, July 10, 2018 AM　\r\n\r\nPIC:　Ms Forgeot\r\nWhen I made an inquiry, I was told that we will not accept meetings other than those of officially recognized international partners, but we can confirm whether it is acceptable. However, the answer was that there were too many requests for visits, and there was no room to accept them due to the lack of staff, so their hopes were very slim.\r\n\r\n= Give up > and contact the Chamber of agriculture of Ile de France region to confirm Ile = de = French Chamber of Agriculture.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n▼YYJO047759-01OCT14 NOKH04 A) CHUOKAI KEIZAIREN　31+1 \r\n\r\nContact person: Ms Florence Forgeot - Economy department assistant\r\nTEL: 　01.53.83.47.35\r\n※ Person in charge of the day\r\nMr Claude Soud&eacute; &#8211; Directeur Adjoint du D&eacute;partement Economie et D&eacute;veloppement durable, Chef de projet PAC/ Affaires  europ&eacute;ennes et internationales.\r\nand Deputy Director of the Division of Economy and Sustainable Development, Chief of PAC Projects/European and International Relations  \r\n\r\nDate: Wednesday, October 8, 2014, 10:00-11:30 a.m. (about one and a half hours)\r\nProgram content: Lecture and Q&A.　\r\nInterview content:\r\n- Introduction and Activities of FNSEA\r\n- About the main agricultural products of France\r\n- The current state of agriculture in France and EU countries.\r\n- Q&A\r\n\r\nCost: Free\r\n* Please prepare a souvenir to return the kindness.\r\n\r\n------------------------------------\r\n\r\n★YYJO038689-28SEP11 NOKH04 A)NOK CHUOKAI KEIZAIREN 10 (GRQ NGO-0065)approx. 30+1\r\n\r\nDate: Tuesday, October 4, 2011, 0930-1100 (about one and a half hours)\r\nContact person: Ms Florence Forgeot - Economy department assistant\r\n※ Person in charge of the day\r\nMr Claude Soud&eacute; &#8211; FNSEA Deputy Director to Agricultural Policies.\r\n\r\n・Inspection Program: Interviews\r\n\r\nInterview content:\r\n- Presentation on FNSEA's role and activities\r\n- About the main agricultural products of France\r\n- The current state of agriculture in France and EU countries.\r\n- Q&A\r\n\r\n※Please※\r\n(1) A list of all participants (name, title, affiliation, and company name are required) must be submitted in advance.\r\n\r\n(2) A questionnaire is not mandatory, but if you have one, please let us know as soon as possible as we will send it to the other party in advance for consideration.\r\n(I told them that I would ask questions during the Q&A session on the day of the ⇒.)\r\n\r\n・Inspection fee: Free. Please prepare a souvenir to return the favor.",
