    "description": "Tayto Crisp was founded in Dublin in 1954 by Joe Murphy. It is currently managed by Largo Foods.\r\n\r\nTayto Crisp invented the process of making the first flavored cheese and onion crisps (potato chips). It is now Ireland's leading producer of crisps, popcorn and other snacks in a variety of flavours.\r\n\r\nIn 2010, a theme park called Tayto Park was built next to the plant. This is Ireland's only theme park, with a variety of attractions, an amusement park, zoo facilities, and factory tours.\r\n\r\n* Crisp = potato chips.",
