    "description": "It is a farm built in 1948 by the Iacchelli brothers. Having cleared 80 hectares of land between Velletri and Genzano near Rome, they are now doing agriturismo business in a modern way, providing their own crops to visitors in the farm's restaurant, while at the same time creating accommodation and providing their guests with their harvest.\r\n\r\nIn addition to farm management, we also conduct a variety of activities such as seminars for the general public on nutrition, herbs, harvests, and the relationship between the environment and agriculture, as well as programs for students.\r\n\r\nOn site there is an animal husbandry, a food production point, a restaurant and accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe wine and meals served at the restaurant basically use ingredients produced by ourselves, so it would be interesting to visit from the perspective of \"local production for local consumption\".\r\n\r\nOpen: TUE-SUN (Closed on MON) at 09.30-17.00",
