    "description": "At Lignarius Restoration School in Rome, students and professionals join a hands-on journey into the world of frescoes, mosaics, and historic wall paintings.\r\n\r\nIn a welcoming studio setting, participants explore ancient techniques through direct practice guided by expert artisans. One workshop focuses on creating tempera paintings inspired by the Sistine Chapel, where group work brings classical designs to life on canvas.\r\n\r\nAnother introduces the art of Roman mosaics, from cutting tiny tesserae to assembling large decorative pieces based on real basilica patterns.\r\n\r\nA third workshop blends the restoration of small objects with mosaic-making, combining traditional knowledge with modern insight.\r\n\r\nThe fresco module explains the history and chemistry behind this enduring technique and gives everyone the chance to test their hand with real materials. The school offers a close-up view of artistic preservation, where learning meets collaboration and history becomes a tactile, creative experience in the heart of Rome.",
