    "description": "Discover the art of the jewellery maker at the Bottega Orafa Paolo Penko in Florence.\r\n\r\nThis workshop will take you through the complex processes of jewellery making, combining tradition and innovation. Learn about the history of the Florentine Fiorino, the coin first minted in 1252, and experience its production first-hand. Watch skilled artisans at work, using techniques handed down through generations, such as the traditional ‘ashlar’ (“bugnato”) technique, inspired by Renaissance architecture. Learn an innovative jewellery-making technique known as ‘del penkato’ that uses a diamond point for intricate engraving and detailing. \r\n\r\nChoose from a range of experiences, including a hands-on workshop to create your own coin or jewellery, or a visit to the Oratorio Mediceo to dmire iconic artefacts. At the end of the tour, you will take home a unique souvenir: a golden replica of the Fiorino, along with its fascinating history.",
