    "description": "In a historic family-run dairy, visitors get to see how Parmigiano Reggiano is made. \r\n\r\nThe tour shows the final production steps inside the maturing warehouses and cheese factory. Cheese wheels are carefully removed from the vats when still soft and then divided into individual wheels.\r\n\r\nThese wheels are placed into molds called “fascera” to give them their shape and prepare them for aging. These steps are essential to achieve the cheese’s characteristic texture and quality. After the tour, visitors taste Parmigiano Reggiano at different aging stages, paired with local Lambrusco wine.\r\n\r\nThe tasting highlights the differences in flavor and texture that develop over time. Guests also have the option to purchase cheese directly from the dairy, ensuring fresh, authentic products.\r\n\r\nThis visit offers a clear look at the traditional process behind one of Italy’s most famous products, all in a welcoming family environment.",
