    "description": "The Taccani hydroelectric power plant in Trezzo sull’Adda offers a unique journey through history, nature, and technology.\r\n\r\nThe visit begins outside with an introduction to the plant’s architecture by Gaetano Moretti and views of the water intake system and two historic turbines displayed in an open-air museum in the garden.\r\n\r\nVisitors learn about the geography of the Adda River and its natural surroundings, setting the stage for understanding the plant’s role in producing clean energy.\r\n\r\nInside, the tour continues in a Liberty-style room housing a historical exhibition and an interactive museum. Visitors then enter the generator room to see the machinery in action and receive an educational explanation of a silent generator from 1906, showcasing early hydroelectric technology.\r\n\r\nThis experience blends technical insights with cultural heritage, offering a clear picture of how water energy has powered the region for over a century.",
