    "description": "Il Paese Ritrovato is a small village where people, in complete safety, live in protected apartments but can move independently in the square, to the café, to the shops and to the cinema, living their life, compatible with the disease, feeling at home and at the same time receiving the necessary attention and care.\r\n\r\nA place where people with dementia are free to choose what to do with their time and find a dimension of sociality that restores value to their life.\r\n\r\nIl Paese Ritrovato is one of the facilities managed by La Meridiana, founded in 1976 as a voluntary association, today it is a social cooperative with 107 volunteers and 331 employees, professionals and consultants and a complete range of services aimed at the elderly.\r\n\r\nAmong others, Day Centers and Aggregation Centers for the elderly, Hospice, Protected Housing all based on quality of life of the residents and new, more specialized and person-centered care models.",
