    "description": "Officina Profumo-Farmaceutica di Santa Maria Novella sets its roots back to 1221.\r\n\r\nFounded as a Dominican friars conventum, it is considered today the oldest pharmacy in the world, which carries its activities in the very places where they all began.\r\n\r\nIts products are prized by royal houses, notable artists and personalities and still made following the artisanal techniques of the Dominican friars. The guided tour includes the different rooms including the museum section, the storage cellars, the herbal tea room and the distillery that overlooks the ancient botanical garden of the friars, open on special occasions.\r\n\r\nDon’t miss the collections of ancient instruments, stills and pharmacy jars made by the ceramics of Montelupo, by Richard-Ginori and by Chini.",
