    "description": "ANCI Associazione Nazionale Comuni Italiani - the National Association of Italian Municipalities is a non-profit association that brings together the large majority of \r\nItaly’s comune (municipalities) - over 7,000 - and serves as their collective representative.\r\n\r\nIts core mission is to represent and defend the interests of Italian municipalities toward the national government, regions and European institutions, support local authorities in administrative issues, public policy, services and territorial development, promote cooperation, best practices, training and engagement between local governments on key topics like digital transformation, sustainability, services, and community welfare.\r\n\r\nDuring the visit, participants gain insight into regional governance and how ANCI fosters collaboration between local authorities, defending local autonomy and promoting sustainable development. Guests have the opportunity to discuss best practices and innovative policies with experienced staff. It is designed for knowledgeable guests interested in public management and territorial \r\ndevelopment.",
    "tourProgramExample": "- Networking with local administrators, civic leaders, and professionals\r\n- A hub where local governments collaborate, \r\ninnovate and influence public policy\r\n- A unique way to interact with local Italian communities \r\nand see diverse regional identities in one place",
