    "description": "A squero is a traditional Venetian boatyard where gondolas and other wooden boats are built, maintained, and restored — a craft that’s part of Venice’s cultural identity.\r\n\r\nThe Squero Tramontin in Dorsoduro district was founded in 1884 by Domenico Tramontin and has been active for almost a century and a half.\r\n\r\nThroughout its history it introduced innovations in gondola design, and it became known for the quality and craftsmanship of its boats.\r\n\r\nSince 2018, the workshop has been run by sisters Elena and Elisabetta Tramontin, preserving the family business and tradition of constructing and restoring gondolas.\r\n\r\nVisiting the Squero Tramontin is very different from visiting a traditional tourist museum — it’s the authentic working space of artisans at work. The Tramontin family and their team still use traditional tools like axes, planes and hammers to shape and assemble the wood.",
