    "description": "Visiting the Consorzio di Tutela del Limone di Siracusa IGP in Siracusa is a unique experience that blends agricultural heritage, food culture, and regional pride.\r\n\r\nThe Consorzio di Tutela del Limone di Siracusa IGP is the official consortium that protects and promotes lemon grown in the Siracusa area under Protected Geographical Indication. It was established in 2000 to safeguard the product’s quality, origins, and traditional cultivation methods.",
    "tourProgramExample": "During the visit of\r\nthe Consortium Headquarters staff will explain about the IGP certification: what\r\nit means, why it matters, and the strict production regulations behind it, the\r\nhistory of lemon cultivation in Siracusa, a tradition that goes back centuries.\r\nHow the Consortium works to protect the name and quality of the lemons,\r\nincluding monitoring markets and enforcing proper use of the IGP label. Touring\r\ntraditional lemon groves and seeing how lemons are grown, harvested, and\r\ntended by local producers. Taste fresh lemons straight from the orchard and\r\nlocal gastronomic products such as lemon granita, limoncello, pastries, gelato\r\nmade with the IGP lemons​",
