    "description": "Tenuta Colombara is a historic rice estate in the Vercelli plain, one of Europe’s most important rice-growing areas. Founded around the 15th century, it evolved from a simple travelers’ hostel into a self-sufficient rural village\r\n\r\nAn authentic experience in the heart of Vercelli's rice fields: visit the Rice Conservatory inside the historic Tenuta Colombara, home of Riso Acquerello in Livorno Ferraris (Vercelli). Walk through the perfectly preserved rooms, the rice weeders' dormitory, the artisan workshops, and the rural school, for a journey back in time to discover 20th-century rural life.\r\n\r\nThe surrounding landscape creates a striking environment that also supports a delicate ecosystem of birds, frogs, and insects.\r\n\r\nRiso Acquerello is a premium Carnaroli rice produced exclusively at Tenuta Colombara, widely considered one of the finest rices in the world due to its unique processing method and exceptional quality, a product that blends tradition, innovation, and gastronomy, highly valued by chefs and gourmet markets worldwide.",
