    "description": "In 1919 a wealthy cloth merchant named Isaia Levi founded Italy’s first cartridge pen factory. In the 1960s, the business was taken over by the Verona family, who still run the factory today.\r\n\r\nAurora fountain pens have become a household name in Italy, and many Italians remember learning to write with an Aurora pen, but Aurora has also become part of the history of design, thanks to cutting-edge models, such as the famous “Hastil”, which was designed by Marco Zanuso and is on display at MOMA in New York.\r\n\r\nA visit to the factory allows you to observe the various stages of production of the iconic Aurora pens, discovering the craftsmanship and passion behind the production of each writing instrument.\r\n\r\nHandcrafted for over a century and now distributed in over 50 countries, they are a global symbol of Made in Italy excellence.",
