    "description": "The administrative and financial reforms of the city of Tilburg, which led to moderate and consensus-oriented reforms, were modeled in Germany and Northern Europe. The administrative and financial reform is known as the \"Tilburg Model\".\r\n\r\nCity of Tilburg:\r\nThe municipality is located about one and a half hours south of Amsterdam.\r\nIt was a thriving textile city, but in the 1960s the textile industry throughout the Netherlands declined and numerous factories closed.  Many of the ruins left in the city were rebuilt as new settlements, and an area lined with distinctive residences was born.\r\nSince then, the industry has diversified, and now having a wide range of companies is considered to be a characteristic of the Tilburg economy.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Full Day Program\r\n\r\n09:00 Meet at City Hall (Greetings from Mayor Tilburg)\r\n09:30-12:30 Presentation on the Tilburg model\r\n12:30-14:00 Lunch\r\n14:00-15:00 Lecture by the person in charge\r\n　　　　　　  -Redevelopment of city center infrastructure\r\n              -Redevelopment of public squares in the city center with private participation\r\n15:00-16:00 Visit to the public square\r\n\r\nThe actual lunch fee was the actual cost, and the inspection fee was free.",
