    "id": "mice-Y2VudHJlIGZvciBpbmZlY3Rp",
    "title": "Centre for Infectious Disease Control (Centrum Infectieziektebestrijding / CIb ), National Institute for Public Health and the Environment ( RIVM / Rijksinstituut voor Volksgezondheid en Milieu )",
    "category": "Technical Visit",
    "targetTourCategories": [],
    "tags": [
      "Healthcare"
    ],
    "description": "The Netherlands Centre for Infectious Disease Control is an institution within the National Institute of Public Health and the Environment. In cooperation with relevant departments of local governments and the government, it is responsible for coordinating all control actions related to infectious diseases, such as effective prevention methods, sufficient alertness, rapid response in the event of an infectious disease outbreak, and efforts to reduce health problems caused by infectious diseases.",
    "tourProgramExample": "**KUONI cannot be arranged / Request via Japan embassy** \r\n\r\n<OSA-0628 MUNICIPALITY DEVELOPMENT TV IN F & NL> \r\n\r\nDue to changes to the rules for accepting visits by Dutch ministries and competent organizations, it is no longer possible to arrange a visit to the Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sports via KUONI, as it will be considered only for requests for visits through official diplomatic channels (Japan embassies). (The same applies to other ministries.) ） \r\n\r\nThe Netherlands National Institute of Public Health and the Public Health Agency, which also requested arrangements, are also national organizations under the ministry, so inquiries from the Japan embassy are also required. \r\n\r\n------------------------------------------ \r\n\r\n<TTAO220795-08NOV17 EAAE01 \"A) SOUZOU-GATA\" (TYO-1490)>\r\n\r\n☆ Date and time \r\n\r\nNovember 13 (Mon) ~ 5 (Wed), 2017 \r\n\r\n☆Number of people \r\n\r\n01~10+Interpretation \r\n\r\n☆ Theme\r\n\r\nInfectious Disease Control\r\n\r\n☆ Answer\r\n\r\nNot accepted because there are no staff available.\r\nSince there are a large number of requests for inspection visits from overseas, and the time burden of the researcher's work is required to respond to inspections, it is necessary to carefully select only a few times a year.\r\n\r\n☆ Refused other parts (internal information)\r\n\r\n- Amsterdam Health Center (GGD Amsterdam) (http://www.ggd.amsterdam.nl/english/)\r\n　→ I also inquired about lifestyle-related diseases in my second choice theme, but the relevant department (Amsterdam Healthy Weight Program) also replied that it was not acceptable.\r\n　→ From here, the Dutch Centre for Infectious Disease Control was proposed.\r\n- Leiden University Medical Center\r\n- Erasmus University Medical Center: no answer\r\n- Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport, Netherlands \r\n  → In the end, I received an acceptable answer, but I gave up because it was the day before departure.\r\n\r\n⇒ I couldn't find a place to accept it, so I changed my theme. (Measures to prevent lifestyle-related diseases, and changed to home-visit nursing and home care.) ）",
    "officialWebsite": "http://www.rivm.nl/en/About_RIVM/Organisation/Centres/Centre_for_Infectious_Disease_Control",
