    "id": "mice-Y2VudHJ1bSBiaW9sb2dpc2No",
    "title": "Centrum Biologische Landbouw (CBL=Centre for Organic Agriculture)",
    "category": "Technical Visit",
    "targetTourCategories": [],
    "tags": [
      "Agriculture"
    ],
    "description": "Center for Organic Agriculture = CBL\r\n\r\nDescription: The province of Flebolant, northeast of Amsterdam, is a new land that has been reclaimed since the 20th century. Organic farming has been practiced in the region since the 1980s.\r\nThe Centre for Organic Farming (CBL) in the provincial capital of Löristadt was established by the Organic Agriculture Association of Flebolant with the aim of promoting organic farming.\r\n\r\nIt is a foundation that aims to revitalize organic farming by promoting bioproduction and organic farming, supporting producers, providing technical guidance and information.\r\n\r\nCBL's main activities (examples)\r\n* Organize farm visits and excursions for students, farmers, traders and other people interested in organic farming.\r\n* Launch and participate in projects that contribute to the development and promotion of the field of organic agriculture.\r\n*Accommodation arrangements for conferences, research and other meetings.\r\n* Organic food catering.\r\n\r\n※※Currently, it is closed and it is not possible to visit the center. (as of 04JAN2016)※※",
    "tourProgramExample": "YYJO045195-02OCT13 NOKH04 A)CHUOKAI KEIZAIREN NL/CH/F 10 (GRQ NGO-0098)31+1 \r\n* Arranged by AgriExperience.\r\n\r\n**Lunch** \r\nRestaurant Wind in de Wilgen \r\nAdd   Bronsweg 2   Lelystad \r\ntel  　0320-281073 \r\nURL      http://www.windindewilgen.nl/\r\n\r\n* A restaurant known for its menu of organically grown vegetables near CBL.\r\n* Lunch time is 1 hour.\r\nSample menu: Meat or fish main dish with rice and vegetables\r\n\r\nDate: Friday, October 4, 2013, 13:30-15:00 (about 1.1.1/2 hours)\r\nContents of the visit: Hearings, Q&A, etc.\r\n*Theme of the interview: Discussion with organic farming in the Netherlands\r\nCBL's activities, the current state of bioproduction and organic farming in the Netherlands, etc.\r\n\r\nCost (tax included): All tax included\r\n◆Inspection (3 locations):\r\nEUR929.50 per group per group.\r\n・ 2 places to visit (agrifarm + chrysanthemum farmer)\r\nEUR 544.50 per group\r\n・1 inspection point (CBL)\r\nEUR385.-per group\r\n\r\n◆Lunch (Wind in de Wilgen)\r\nEUR18.-pp per person \r\n\r\n★postscript★\r\n* Inspection is per group (21% tax included).\r\n* Lunch fee is per person (6% tax included). TL, no free interpretation.\r\n\r\n※Cancellation charge:\r\nFrom the date of visit,\r\n・No Charge up to 4 weeks in advance. \r\n・ EUR 50 + VAT 21% 4-2 weeks ago.\r\n・2-1 week before, EUR100 + VAT 21%.\r\n・Full amount within 1 week.\r\n★ This is original.\r\nPD procedures are required, so please guide us ahead of schedule.\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n*TTAO101609-02NOV12 NOKC06 A) MINAMIMAKI-MURA TOUR 17+1 \r\n\r\n・Date and time: Tuesday, November 6, 2012, 0930-1230 + lunch 1300-1400\r\n・Program:\r\n9.30-11.00 Hearing about bioproduction and organic farming at CBL Organic Agriculture Center\r\n\r\n11.00-12.30 Bio-producer farmer \"Arenosa\"\r\n  biological farm \"Arenosa\"\r\n  Address    Jupiterweg 9, 8211 AW Lelystad\r\n  tel     　 0320-234067\r\n  -Rare proprietary vegetables (dipterocarps, parsnips, jerusalem artichoke, etc.) are grown by hand with high-tech equipment equipped with GPS.\r\n  * November is not the season, so the amount of vegetables in the arable land is small,\r\n    You can see the vegetables when washing and packing them after harvest.\r\n\r\n13.00–14.00: Lunch Biological Lunch\r\n  Restaurant Wind in de Wilgen\r\n  Address   Bronsweg 2   Lelystad\r\n  tel     　0320-281073\r\n  URL       http://www.windindewilgen.nl/\r\n  We serve dishes using organically grown vegetables.\r\n  * This restaurant serves rice and seasonal vegetables in a Japanese style to suit the tastes of Japan people.\r\n\r\n【Inspection fee (tax included)】\r\nEUR 1,775.10.- (including 21% VAT) for 6 locations and 3 days: Group\r\n*Lunch fee will be charged separately from EUR 18.00 per person (including 6% VAT).\r\n\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n＊YJO031675-30SEP09 NOKH04 A) NOK CHUOKAI KEIZAIREN TV (GRQ NGO-0024) 32+1\r\n・Contact: Mrs Jenny Pannenbecker (same person as last time in 2008)\r\n・Date and time: Thursday, October 1, 2009, 1230-1500\r\n・Program: Lunch and hearing\r\n　12:30-13:30 Lunch (at the restaurant)\r\n　13:45-15:00 Hearing about organic farming\r\n\r\n■Lunch\r\nRestaurant Wind in de Wilgen\r\nAddress: Bronsweg 25, Lelystad\r\nTEL:0320-281073\r\n\r\n< lunch menu>\r\n-Clear chicken soup with carrot and taug&eacute;\r\n-Rice\r\n-Grilled courgette\r\n-Salad of raw vegetables\r\n-Bread with cheese and ham\r\n-Hot vegetables in oyster sauce\r\n(90% use organically grown products.) ）\r\n\r\n■Hearing about Dutch organic farming at CBL\r\n  - Activities of CBL, CBL's contribution to organic agriculture\r\n  - Current state of organic farming in the Netherlands\r\n  - Needs and pricing for organic vegetables and organic foods in the EU\r\n\r\n■Inspection fee (tax included)\r\nEUR1,300 per group\r\n* Includes lunch fee.\r\n* Calculated by 32 people + tour conductor. (Lunch by interpreter is also included)\r\n\r\n★Arrangements through Agriexperience.\r\n\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n*YYJO029326-01OCT08 NOKH04 A) FROM NOKYO CHUOKAI KEIZAIREN TV\r\n\r\n(1) Presentation about the Organic Farming Center (about 1 hour)\r\nFarm visit (approx. 1.5 hours)\r\n\r\n(2) Wednesday, October 2, 2008 29+1t/l\r\n\r\nby Mrs Jenny Pannenbecker\r\n・(About 1 hour) Lunch\r\n・(About 45 minutes) Hearing about organic farming\r\n・ (About 1 hour) Accompanied by an organic agriculture center, visit the following farmers\r\nCULTIVATOR :D E KEMPHAAN\r\nAddress :Kemphaanpad 14, 1358 AC Almere　\r\nTel. :+31 365 384 262\r\nPerson in charge :Mrs Tineke van den Berg\r\nWeb :http://home.kpn.nl/ber01950/home.html\r\n\r\nEstablished 1996\r\nTineke van den Berg / Tom Saat\r\nArea: 600 hectares\r\nHandling onions, peas, cabbage, beef\r\n\r\nWe are a farmer who also handles biological crops,\r\nIt also plays a role as an educational farm for the general public.\r\n\r\nInspection fee (all tax included): Lunch fee EUR 627.-(32PAX), CBL lecture fee EUR 450.- Farmer visit EUR 310.-\r\n\r\n===========================\r\n★ Prepayment is required in full for all destinations visited due to arrangements made through a supplier (AgriExperience) for the Dutch agricultural tour. \r\n<Examples of expenses>\r\nThe inspection fee for each visit varies depending on the content (difficulty), but it starts from about EUR 270.- (tax included) per group location. The total may differ slightly, but please consider this as a guide. \r\n*2008 Basic Rate (per TV location): EUR 225.00 + VAT (19%) = EUR 267.75",
