    "title": "Olij Rozen (Rose Farm)",
    "category": "Technical Visit",
    "targetTourCategories": [],
    "tags": [
      "Agriculture"
    ],
    "description": "A major general production company of roses in the Netherlands. With a cultivation area of 6 hectares, we are engaged in rose cut flower production, breeding research, seedling production, and sales. It is also well established in breeding varieties of roses. Roses grown in greenhouses are exported as cut flowers abroad or shipped to major domestic fresh flower markets.\r\n\r\nWe started in 1980 with the cultivation of cut roses, and in 2004 we also started growing potted roses.",
    "tourProgramExample": "<FUK-0197 AGRI & HORTICULTURAL TVs IN D/NL ( Kagoshima Prefectural College of Agriculture - Agriculture >)\r\n\r\nAs of late May 2017, there is no change in the situation where inspections are not possible at rose farmers.\r\nIt is forbidden for all rose growers in the Netherlands to receive guests, because of hygienic reasons for the plants. Last year a bacteria was found and all rose growers had to close their doors to protect their plants.\r\n\r\n---------------------------------------\r\n\r\n<YYJO056023-22OCT17 NOKH04 \"AI) AICHI NOGYOHOUJIN 7\" (NGO-0166)> SURVEY\r\n\r\nAs a defense against the 2016 outbreak of bacterial wilt, the majority of rose farmers in the Netherlands are currently not allowed outsiders to enter their greenhouses.\r\n\r\nTherefore, it is not possible to arrange cultivation site tours, especially in medium- and large-scale facilities.\r\n\r\n---------------------------------------\r\n\r\n<TTAO003815-07OCT07 NTAD09 HORTI FAIR > Arrangement \r\n\r\nOct. 2007\r\nContact Name: Mr P. VEYS\r\n\r\n09:30 - 10:30\r\n- Welcome speech by the farm manager\r\n- Tour of the park\r\n- Q & A Session\r\n\r\nInspection fee (tax included): EUR 1050 per group incl. VAT (total of 7 TVs via AgriExperience)\r\n\r\n---------------------------------------\r\n\r\n<TTJO962313-03OCT05 TKKE11 A) TOCHIGI SEINEN NOGYOSHA (JTGRQ-36C)> arrangement\r\n\r\nDate of visit: October 5, 2005, 1000-1115 a.m.\r\nPic: Mr. Ruud Olij\r\n\r\nInspection fee (tax included): 150 Euros per group (via AgriExperience)",
