    "description": "We offer walking tours and school trips to see the latest urban developments and architecture in the Netherlands and Germany.\r\n\r\nA knowledgeable guide will show you the featured sites and architecture.",
    "tourProgramExample": "<TTAO185107-15NOV15 KHTE07 \"A) NIHON SOGO JUSEIKATSU\">\r\n\r\n☆ Date and time \r\n\r\nThursday, November 19, 2015　 \r\n\r\n☆Number of people \r\n\r\n5+ Interpretation \r\n\r\n☆ミLocation\r\n\r\nLunch Restaurant \"De Kroonprince\"\r\n\r\n☆ Program \r\n\r\nAmsterdam Eiburg Architecture Tour\r\n- Meet at a restaurant at 1330 and transfer to IBURG (by Kuonii bus)\r\n- Upon arrival, tour and explanation of the area\r\n\r\n< topic>　\r\nUrban and residential development of landfills, urban structures, floating homes, places to work/live, sustainability, etc.\r\n< are some examples of highlights>　\r\n- Blok 14 by DKV and Kempe Thill \r\n- Shopping centre and housing by Lucas Ellermann van Vugt, KZG and Arons en Gelauff \r\n- Housing by KSK, by De Architecten Cie., VMX architects and de Architectengroep,by Claus+Kaan, by Maccreanor Lavington Architects\r\n- Floating houses by Marlies Rohmer, etc.\r\n\r\nThe visiting language is Dutch.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDuration: 4 hours\r\n\r\nProgram: A tour of the redevelopment area, a guide by an architect who talks not only about the architecture itself, but also about its background (e.g. the history of Amsterdam's development, urban planning, infrastructure, traffic and parking problems).\r\nYou'll visit Silodam, Ijburg and the Eastern Harbour Redevelopment Area by bus, and through the canals to Q-park (parking lots only).\r\n \r\nFee: €750 (per 4-5 people)\r\n\r\n-------------------------------------\r\n\r\n< GRQ TYO-0085> Survey\r\n\r\nEastern Harbour District Tour\r\nhttp://www.archex.info/english/netherlands/amsterdam_eastern_docklands_borneo_sporenburg_java_knsm.html　\r\nAmsterdam East Gulf: KNSM Island, Java and Borneo Sporlenburg will guide you through the latest architectural complexes, residential, business and commercial district developments in about 2h30.\r\nCost: EUR360.00 incl VAT p/group",
