    "description": "Information only (no inspection arrangements)***\r\n\r\nDesigned by Amsterdam-based architects Mejel and van Schooten, the building is the former headquarters of international financial firm ING Bank. It is famous in the Netherlands for winning numerous awards, including the Aluminum Awards and the National Steel Prize 2002.\r\n\r\nThe building is 28x138m, 10 floors high (about 48m), and the total site area is 5,600 square meters. It rests on 16 support bars with a height of 9m~12m, which is similar to the structure of the bridge.\r\n\r\nThe exterior wall blocks noise from nearby highways and draws filtered clean air into the room.\r\n\r\nThe headquarters building houses boardrooms, executive offices, and many corporate divisions. It is nicknamed \"Money Shoes\" after the design of the bank and its building.\r\n\r\n[Reference: Netherlands National Tourist Board]",
