    "tags": [
      "Administration"
    ],
    "description": "In 1978, the Gender Equality Act was enacted, prohibiting gender discrimination in all areas of society and stating that administrative authorities and employers have the responsibility to actively promote gender equality within their respective responsibilities. In 1997, the Center for Gender Equality was established as an independent body to implement this law.\r\n\r\nThe center was renamed the Gender Equality and Discrimination Ombud in 2006 and responds free of charge to complaints about gender equality violations. In addition to promoting gender equality in society, the Ombud also documents and provides information on various cases of discrimination and counseling on racial issues related to employment.",
    "tourProgramExample": "Training Project \"Gender Equality\"\r\nThe meeting was held on the following themes: (Time required: 2 hours)\r\n　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　\r\n- The current state of gender in Norway　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　\r\n- Women's participation and leadership in politics　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　\r\n- Gender equality and anti-discrimination activities　 　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　\r\n- Q&A　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　          \r\n*Lunch meeting after that (from 11:30)　　　\r\n\r\nThe inspection fee was free.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n\r\nTime required: About 1 hour\r\n\r\nLecture by the person in charge\r\n・Explanation of the Institute\r\n・Activities to promote gender equality\r\n\r\nThe inspection fee was free.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n\r\nYou will receive a lecture on the contents of the activities. \r\n2-hour lecture, NOK2000 (group rate/29 people) \r\nWebsite of the predecessor Center for Gender Equality - http://www.likestilling.no/english/",
