    "description": "It is a partnership with the UK government's Urban Renewal Authority whose main purpose is to promote high-quality, sustainable growth in England.\r\n\r\n⇒ On December 1, 2008, it was reorganized under the jurisdiction of the Homes & Communities Agency. (This data is from an inspection arrangement in October 2008 on the theme of the UK Public Housing Revitalization and Housing Action Trusts.) ）\r\n\r\nAbout Housing Action Trusts (HATS)\r\n\r\nHousing Action Trusts (HATS) is one of the residential estate revitalization and community revitalization projects in the United Kingdom. (The six Housing Action Trusts that were implemented have already been dismantled.) ）\r\nWhen it was first introduced by the revision of the Housing Act in 1998, it met with opposition from local governments and residents as a centralized method, but since then it has changed to a partnership type that requires and premises the cooperation of local governments and residents. Since then, it has been regarded as one of the culmination of housing estates and regional revitalization methods in the UK, including a mechanism of thorough public participation, a multifaceted approach to the revitalization of difficult housing estates and regions, and financial measures to realize both.",
    "tourProgramExample": "<TTQF001922-12OCT'08 TCID01 A) KASSEIKA - LON> Arrangement Example *TV is CXL*\r\n\r\nSample hearing (approx. 2 hours):\r\non the regeneration of social housing and projects in London, particularly the Thames Gateway reclaimed area.\r\n\r\nThe inspection fee was free.\r\n\r\n⇒ After the arrangements were confirmed, the person in charge of the inspection became inconvenient (after the end of the summer recess of the Diet, serious topics were raised in various directions, and we were forced to attend the meeting on that side + the merger with two other non-governmental organizations was decided, and the problems related to the organizations themselves around the English Partnerships increased), so the customer did not actually visit.",
