    "description": "This data is from an inspection arrangement in October 2008 on the theme of Housing Action Trusts (HATS) in the UK Public Housing Revitalization. We visited one of the HATS, the revitalization project of Stonebridge in the borough of Brent.\r\n\r\n* According to the English Partnerships website, the HATS was completed in 2007, but as of October 2008, we received information that the project itself is currently in progress.\r\n\r\nAbout Housing Action Trusts (HATS) \r\n\r\nHousing Action Trusts (HATS) is one of the residential estate revitalization and community revitalization projects in the United Kingdom. (The six Housing Action Trusts that were implemented have already been dismantled.) ） \r\nWhen it was first introduced by the revision of the Housing Act in 1998, it met with opposition from local governments and residents as a centralized method, but since then it has changed to a partnership type that requires and premises the cooperation of local governments and residents. Since then, it has been regarded as one of the culmination of housing estates and regional revitalization methods in the UK, including a mechanism of thorough public participation, a multifaceted approach to the revitalization of difficult housing estates and regions, and financial measures to realize both.",
    "tourProgramExample": "<TTQF001922-12OCT'08 TCID01 A) KASSEIKA - LON>\r\n\r\nExample of the visit (about 2 hours): \r\nHearing and site tour. (Including an explanation of the history of this HATS, the Stonebridge Regeneration Project, the current situation and future plans, etc.) ）\r\n\r\nThe inspection fee was free.",
